var e={id:`united-states`,name:`United States`,flag:`🇺🇸`,currency:`USD`,language:`English`,greeting:{text:`Howdy`,meaning:`Hello (informal, short for "how do you do")`},bestMonths:[4,5,6,9,10],tips:[`Tipping is expected: 18–22% at sit-down restaurants, $1–2 per drink at bars, and 15–20% for taxis and rideshares.`,`Listed prices usually exclude sales tax (about 8.9% in NYC, 8.6% in San Francisco), which is added at the register.`,`In New York, tap a contactless card or phone at OMNY readers on subways and buses; in San Francisco, use Clipper (also on your phone) for Muni, BART and cable cars.`,`Most visitors from visa-waiver countries need an approved ESTA before flying; apply online well ahead of travel.`,`Distances inside a city are walkable, but cities are far apart; fly between coasts (about 6 hours) rather than drive.`],cities:[{id:`new-york`,name:`New York City`,lat:40.7128,lng:-74.006,timezone:`America/New_York`,tagline:`Skyscrapers, Broadway lights and a slice on every corner`,description:`A relentless, walkable city of world-class museums, iconic skylines and neighbourhoods that each feel like a different town. Days start in Central Park and end under the neon of Times Square or in a basement jazz club.`,idealDays:[4,6],places:[{id:`statue-of-liberty`,name:`Statue of Liberty & Ellis Island`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`ferry`,`history`,`viewpoint`],area:`Lower Manhattan`,lat:40.6892,lng:-74.0445,durationHours:4.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:5,description:`Lady Liberty on her island in the harbour, paired with the moving Ellis Island immigration museum on the same ferry loop from Battery Park.`,tip:`Buy only from Statue City Cruises (the official seller); pedestal and crown access sell out weeks to months ahead, and security is airport-style.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Statue of Liberty`},{id:`staten-island-ferry`,name:`Staten Island Ferry`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`free`,`ferry`,`sunset`,`night-view`,`skyline`],area:`Lower Manhattan`,lat:40.7014,lng:-74.0131,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A free 25-minute commuter ferry that glides past the Statue of Liberty with sweeping Manhattan skyline views.`,tip:`Stand on the right side heading out for the Statue; you must disembark at St. George and re-board for the return.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Staten Island Ferry`},{id:`9-11-memorial-museum`,name:`9/11 Memorial & Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`memorial`,`rainy-day`],area:`Lower Manhattan`,lat:40.7115,lng:-74.0134,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:36,rating:4,description:`Twin reflecting pools mark the footprints of the Twin Towers, while the underground museum tells the story of September 11 with quiet power.`,tip:`The outdoor memorial pools are free; book timed museum tickets online and allow time for an emotional visit.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`National September 11 Memorial & Museum`},{id:`brooklyn-bridge`,name:`Brooklyn Bridge`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`free`,`walk`,`viewpoint`,`photo`],area:`Lower Manhattan`,lat:40.7061,lng:-73.9969,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`Walk the 1883 stone-and-cable bridge on its elevated wooden promenade for classic views of the Manhattan skyline.`,tip:`Go early morning to beat crowds, start in Manhattan and walk toward Brooklyn so the skyline is behind you for photos at the end, and stay out of the bike lane.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Brooklyn Bridge`},{id:`brooklyn-bridge-park`,name:`Brooklyn Bridge Park & DUMBO`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`free`,`waterfront`,`sunset`,`kids`,`photo`],area:`DUMBO`,lat:40.702,lng:-73.9967,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Waterfront lawns, piers and Jane's Carousel with front-row views of Lower Manhattan, plus the cobbled DUMBO streets framing the Manhattan Bridge.`,tip:`Snap the famous Manhattan Bridge shot at Washington St & Water St, then stay for sunset over the skyline.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Brooklyn Bridge Park`},{id:`katz-delicatessen`,name:`Katz's Delicatessen`,category:`food`,tags:[`deli`,`pastrami`,`iconic`,`rainy-day`],area:`Lower East Side`,lat:40.7223,lng:-73.9874,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:32,rating:4,description:`Since 1888, this cavernous deli has piled hand-carved pastrami sky-high on rye; one sandwich easily feeds two.`,tip:`Hold on to the ticket you get at the door; losing it means a fee on the way out. Tip the carver a dollar or two for a tasting slice.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Katz's Delicatessen`},{id:`soho-shopping`,name:`SoHo`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`boutiques`,`architecture`,`cast-iron`],area:`SoHo`,lat:40.7233,lng:-74.003,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Cobblestone streets lined with cast-iron facades house flagship stores, designer boutiques and galleries.`,tip:`Broadway is chain-heavy; the side streets like Greene, Mercer and Prince hold the more interesting shops.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`SoHo, Manhattan`},{id:`village-vanguard`,name:`Village Vanguard`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`jazz`,`live-music`,`historic`,`rainy-day`],area:`Greenwich Village`,lat:40.736,lng:-74.0017,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:50,rating:4,description:`A tiny, legendary basement jazz club open since 1935, where Coltrane and Bill Evans recorded classic live albums.`,tip:`Reserve online for a set (usually 8pm and 10pm); there is a one-drink minimum on top of the cover.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Village Vanguard`},{id:`the-high-line`,name:`The High Line`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`walk`,`park`,`architecture`,`iconic`],area:`Chelsea`,lat:40.748,lng:-74.0048,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`An elevated rail line turned into a 1.45-mile garden walk, threading between buildings from the Meatpacking District to Hudson Yards.`,tip:`Start at Gansevoort St and walk north, then drop down to Chelsea Market for lunch.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`High Line`},{id:`chelsea-market`,name:`Chelsea Market`,category:`food`,tags:[`food-hall`,`rainy-day`,`kids`],area:`Chelsea`,lat:40.7424,lng:-74.0061,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`A former Nabisco factory turned food hall packed with tacos, lobster rolls, doughnuts and specialty shops.`,tip:`Weekday mornings are calmer; it is right beside the High Line's 16th St entrance.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Chelsea Market`},{id:`empire-state-building`,name:`Empire State Building`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`viewpoint`,`night-view`,`art-deco`,`rainy-day`],area:`Midtown`,lat:40.7484,lng:-73.9857,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:48,rating:4,description:`The Art Deco icon's open-air 86th-floor deck offers 360-degree views, and the building stays open late for glittering night panoramas.`,tip:`It is open until 2am; late-night visits after 10pm are usually the least crowded.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Empire State Building`},{id:`top-of-the-rock`,name:`Top of the Rock`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`sunset`,`night-view`],area:`Midtown`,lat:40.7593,lng:-73.9794,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`Rockefeller Center's 70th-floor terraces frame both Central Park and the Empire State Building in one sweeping view.`,tip:`Sunset slots cost more and sell out; book a time about 45 minutes before sunset to see day, dusk and night.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`30 Rockefeller Plaza`},{id:`times-square`,name:`Times Square`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`free`,`night-view`,`neon`],area:`Theater District`,lat:40.758,lng:-73.9855,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The blazing, crowded crossroads of Broadway and Seventh Avenue, best experienced after dark when the screens are at full wattage.`,tip:`Sit on the red steps above the TKTS booth for the view, and ignore costumed characters who expect tips for photos.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Times Square`},{id:`broadway-show`,name:`Broadway Show`,category:`culture`,tags:[`iconic`,`theater`,`musical`,`rainy-day`],area:`Theater District`,lat:40.759,lng:-73.9866,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:130,rating:5,description:`World-class musicals and plays in historic theatres clustered around Times Square; seeing a show is a quintessential NYC night.`,tip:`For discounts, try the TKTS booth in Duffy Square for same-day seats or digital lotteries/rush on the show apps. Most theatres are dark on Mondays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Broadway theatre`},{id:`grand-central-terminal`,name:`Grand Central Terminal`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`free`,`architecture`,`beaux-arts`,`rainy-day`],area:`Midtown`,lat:40.7527,lng:-73.9772,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A Beaux-Arts rail hub with a celestial ceiling over its Main Concourse and a famous Whispering Gallery outside the Oyster Bar.`,tip:`Stand in opposite corners of the tiled archway by the Oyster Bar and whisper into the wall; your friend will hear you clearly.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Grand Central Terminal`},{id:`moma`,name:`Museum of Modern Art (MoMA)`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`modern-art`,`rainy-day`],area:`Midtown`,lat:40.7614,lng:-73.9776,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`Van Gogh's The Starry Night, Warhol's soup cans and Monet's Water Lilies headline one of the world's great modern art collections.`,tip:`Book a timed ticket online and head straight to the fifth floor for the most famous works before crowds build.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Museum of Modern Art`},{id:`central-park`,name:`Central Park`,category:`nature`,tags:[`iconic`,`free`,`park`,`kids`,`walk`],area:`Central Park`,lat:40.7829,lng:-73.9654,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`An 843-acre green heart with Bethesda Terrace, Bow Bridge, Strawberry Fields and boating on The Lake.`,tip:`Rent a bike or rowboat at Loeb Boathouse, and enter at 72nd St on the west side for Strawberry Fields.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Central Park`},{id:`metropolitan-museum-of-art`,name:`The Metropolitan Museum of Art`,category:`museum`,tags:[`iconic`,`art`,`rainy-day`,`rooftop`],area:`Upper East Side`,lat:40.7794,lng:-73.9632,durationHours:3.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:5,description:`Five thousand years of art under one vast roof, from the Temple of Dendur to Vermeer, armour and Impressionist masterpieces.`,tip:`Closed Wednesdays; open until 9pm on Fridays and Saturdays. Pick two or three wings rather than trying to see everything.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Metropolitan Museum of Art`},{id:`american-museum-of-natural-history`,name:`American Museum of Natural History`,category:`family`,tags:[`kids`,`dinosaurs`,`science`,`rainy-day`],area:`Upper West Side`,lat:40.7813,lng:-73.974,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:28,rating:4,description:`Towering dinosaur skeletons, the giant blue whale and the dazzling Gilder Center make this a hit with all ages.`,tip:`Book timed entry online; the planetarium show and special exhibits cost extra and are worth adding for kids.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`American Museum of Natural History`},{id:`coney-island`,name:`Coney Island`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`beach`,`roller-coaster`,`kids`,`boardwalk`,`summer`],area:`Coney Island`,lat:40.5744,lng:-73.9786,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:3,description:`Retro seaside fun with a boardwalk, beach, the 1927 wooden Cyclone coaster and Nathan's Famous hot dogs.`,tip:`Rides operate roughly late March to October; take the D, F, N or Q train to the end of the line (about an hour from Midtown).`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Coney Island`},{id:`guggenheim`,name:`Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`architecture`,`rainy-day`],area:`Upper East Side`,lat:40.783,lng:-73.959,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`Frank Lloyd Wright's white spiral on Fifth Avenue, where modern and contemporary art lines a single ramp curling up to a skylight.`,tip:`Take the elevator to the top and stroll down the ramp so gravity does the work.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum`},{id:`one-world-observatory`,name:`One World Observatory`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`skyline`,`rainy-day`,`night-view`],area:`Lower Manhattan`,lat:40.713,lng:-74.0132,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`Floors 100–102 of One World Trade Center, the tallest building in the Western Hemisphere, reached by a 47-second elevator ride through a time-lapse of the city.`,tip:`Pair it with the 9/11 Memorial next door; clear late afternoons give daylight and city lights in one visit.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`One World Observatory`},{id:`summit-one-vanderbilt`,name:`SUMMIT One Vanderbilt`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`immersive`,`sunset`,`night-view`],area:`Midtown`,lat:40.753,lng:-73.9786,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`A mirrored, art-installation take on the observation deck beside Grand Central, with glass ledges hanging over Madison Avenue.`,tip:`Sunset slots sell out first; skip skirts (the floors are mirrors) and wear sunglasses on bright days.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`One Vanderbilt`},{id:`washington-square-park`,name:`Washington Square Park`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`free`,`people-watching`,`street-performers`],area:`Greenwich Village`,lat:40.7308,lng:-73.9973,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The Village's bohemian living room: a marble arch, a splashing fountain, chess hustlers, buskers and NYU students sprawled on every bench.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Washington Square Park`},{id:`essex-market`,name:`Essex Market`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`food-hall`,`rainy-day`,`local`],area:`Lower East Side`,lat:40.7184,lng:-73.9879,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`A century-old municipal market reborn in a bright modern hall, mixing butchers, cheesemongers and bakeries with stalls for tacos, dumplings and bagels.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Essex Market`},{id:`tenement-museum`,name:`Tenement Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`immigration`,`guided-tour`,`rainy-day`],area:`Lower East Side`,lat:40.7188,lng:-73.9901,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:4,description:`Guided tours through restored apartments at 97 Orchard Street tell the real stories of the immigrant families who crammed into them.`,tip:`Visits are by small guided tour only and regularly sell out; book online a few days ahead.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Tenement Museum`},{id:`the-cloisters`,name:`The Met Cloisters`,category:`museum`,tags:[`medieval`,`art`,`gardens`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Washington Heights`,lat:40.8649,lng:-73.9319,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`The Met's medieval branch, built from pieces of European monasteries on a hilltop in Fort Tryon Park, home to the Unicorn Tapestries and herb-scented cloister gardens.`,tip:`A Met ticket covers same-day entry to both the main museum and the Cloisters; take the A train to 190th St.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`The Cloisters`},{id:`new-york-public-library`,name:`New York Public Library (Stephen A. Schwarzman Building)`,category:`culture`,tags:[`free`,`architecture`,`rainy-day`,`library`],area:`Midtown`,lat:40.7532,lng:-73.9822,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The Beaux-Arts flagship guarded by the lions Patience and Fortitude, with the vast, chandeliered Rose Main Reading Room upstairs.`,tip:`Bryant Park, right behind the library, has free table seating, a carousel and a winter ice rink.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`New York Public Library Main Branch`},{id:`williamsburg`,name:`Williamsburg`,category:`culture`,tags:[`neighbourhood`,`vintage`,`bars`,`skyline`],area:`Williamsburg`,lat:40.7171,lng:-73.9566,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Brooklyn's creative hub of vintage stores, record shops, breweries and rooftop bars, with Manhattan skyline views from Domino Park on the waterfront.`,tip:`Take the L train one stop from Manhattan to Bedford Ave, or the NYC Ferry to North Williamsburg.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Williamsburg, Brooklyn`},{id:`little-island`,name:`Little Island`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`park`,`sunset`,`architecture`],area:`Chelsea`,lat:40.742,lng:-74.0103,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A whimsical park floating on tulip-shaped concrete pillars over the Hudson, with winding paths, lawns and a small amphitheatre for summer shows.`,tip:`Combine with a walk along the High Line, whose southern end is a few blocks away.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Little Island at Pier 55`},{id:`comedy-cellar`,name:`Comedy Cellar`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`comedy`,`late-night`,`rainy-day`,`iconic`],area:`Greenwich Village`,lat:40.7302,lng:-74.0005,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`A cramped MacDougal Street basement that is New York's most famous stand-up room, where big-name comics often drop in unannounced.`,tip:`Reserve online several days ahead; there is a cover charge plus a two-item food or drink minimum.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Comedy Cellar`},{id:`intrepid-museum`,name:`Intrepid Museum`,category:`family`,tags:[`ships`,`aviation`,`kids`,`rainy-day`],area:`Hell's Kitchen`,lat:40.7645,lng:-73.9996,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:38,rating:4,description:`An aircraft carrier moored on the Hudson, its flight deck lined with fighter jets, plus a submarine, a Concorde and the Space Shuttle Enterprise.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Intrepid Museum`},{id:`bronx-zoo`,name:`Bronx Zoo`,category:`family`,tags:[`zoo`,`animals`,`kids`],area:`The Bronx`,lat:40.8506,lng:-73.8769,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:4,description:`One of the largest city zoos in the world, with gorillas in the Congo forest, tigers, a monorail through Wild Asia and leafy paths along the Bronx River.`,tip:`General admission is pay-what-you-wish on Wednesdays (reserve online); arrive at opening when the animals are most active.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Bronx Zoo`},{id:`lincoln-center`,name:`Lincoln Center`,category:`culture`,tags:[`opera`,`ballet`,`classical-music`,`rainy-day`],area:`Upper West Side`,lat:40.7725,lng:-73.9835,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:90,rating:4,description:`The campus of the Metropolitan Opera, New York City Ballet and New York Philharmonic, whose fountain plaza glows before curtain-up.`,tip:`The Met Opera sells discounted rush seats for many performances through its website and app on the day.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Lincoln Center`},{id:`aire-ancient-baths`,name:`AIRE Ancient Baths`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`spa`,`thermal-baths`,`rainy-day`,`couples`],area:`Tribeca`,lat:40.7181,lng:-74.004,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:150,rating:4,description:`Candle-lit thermal pools of varying temperatures in a converted 1880s Tribeca textile factory, with a salt-water flotarium and optional massages.`,tip:`Sessions are timed and book up on weekends; weekday afternoons are calmest.`,indoor:!0},{id:`storm-king-art-center`,name:`Storm King Art Center`,category:`culture`,tags:[`day-trip`,`sculpture`,`outdoors`,`hudson-valley`],area:`Hudson Valley`,lat:41.425,lng:-74.0597,durationHours:7,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:28,rating:4,description:`Monumental sculptures by Calder, Serra and Goldsworthy spread across 500 acres of rolling Hudson Valley meadows and hills.`,tip:`Timed tickets are required and the site closes in winter; rent a bike on site to cover the grounds.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Storm King Art Center`},{id:`roosevelt-island-tramway`,name:`Roosevelt Island Tramway`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`night-view`,`cheap`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Upper East Side`,lat:40.7612,lng:-73.9643,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:3,rating:3,description:`An aerial cable car that swings alongside the Queensboro Bridge over the East River for the price of a subway ride.`,tip:`It accepts OMNY and MetroCard like the subway; ride at dusk and stroll to Four Freedoms Park at the island tip.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Roosevelt Island Tramway`},{id:`chinatown-manhattan`,name:`Chinatown`,category:`food`,tags:[`dim-sum`,`street-food`,`cheap-eats`,`neighbourhood`],area:`Chinatown`,lat:40.7158,lng:-73.998,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`Crowded streets of dumpling counters, roast-duck windows, herbal shops and bakeries, centred on Mott, Pell and crooked Doyers Street.`,tip:`Nom Wah Tea Parlor on Doyers Street has served dim sum since 1920.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Chinatown, Manhattan`}],foods:[{name:`New York-style pizza`,description:`Thin, foldable slices with a crisp-chewy crust; grab one from a classic slice joint for a few dollars.`},{name:`Bagel with lox and schmear`,description:`A boiled-then-baked bagel loaded with cream cheese, smoked salmon, capers and red onion.`},{name:`Pastrami on rye`,description:`Hand-carved, peppery smoked brisket piled high with mustard, the signature of Jewish delis.`},{name:`New York cheesecake`,description:`Dense, rich and creamy cheesecake on a graham cracker base.`},{name:`Halal cart chicken over rice`,description:`Street-cart chicken and rice drenched in white sauce and hot sauce, a cheap late-night staple.`},{name:`Black-and-white cookie`,description:`A soft, cakey cookie iced half in vanilla fondant and half in chocolate.`}]},{id:`san-francisco`,name:`San Francisco`,lat:37.7749,lng:-122.4194,timezone:`America/Los_Angeles`,tagline:`Fog, cable cars and the Golden Gate on the bay`,description:`A compact, hilly city of colourful neighbourhoods, bay views and an outstanding food scene. Pack layers: summer fog keeps it cool, while September and October are often the warmest months.`,idealDays:[3,4],places:[{id:`golden-gate-bridge`,name:`Golden Gate Bridge`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`free`,`walk`,`viewpoint`,`photo`],area:`Presidio`,lat:37.8078,lng:-122.475,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`Walk or cycle across the 1.7-mile Art Deco span in International Orange for wind-whipped views of the bay and city.`,tip:`Fog often lifts by midday; for the classic postcard shot, head to Battery Spencer on the Marin side.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Golden Gate Bridge`},{id:`lands-end`,name:`Lands End Trail & Sutro Baths`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`hiking`,`coast`,`sunset`,`ruins`],area:`Outer Richmond`,lat:37.7798,lng:-122.5115,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A rugged clifftop trail with cypress trees, shipwreck coves and surprise Golden Gate views, ending at the ruins of the Sutro Baths.`,tip:`Start at the Lands End Lookout visitor center and stay for sunset over the Pacific.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Lands End (San Francisco)`},{id:`golden-gate-park`,name:`Golden Gate Park`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`park`,`gardens`,`kids`,`bike`],area:`Golden Gate Park`,lat:37.7694,lng:-122.4862,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Larger than Central Park, with the Japanese Tea Garden, Conservatory of Flowers, bison paddock and car-free JFK Promenade.`,tip:`Rent a bike to cover the three miles to Ocean Beach; the Japanese Tea Garden charges a small entry fee.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Golden Gate Park`},{id:`de-young-museum`,name:`de Young Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`architecture`,`viewpoint`,`rainy-day`],area:`Golden Gate Park`,lat:37.7715,lng:-122.4687,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`American, African and Oceanic art in a striking copper-clad building inside Golden Gate Park.`,tip:`The Hamon Observation Tower on the 9th floor is free to visit and has panoramic city views. Closed Mondays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`De Young Museum`},{id:`california-academy-of-sciences`,name:`California Academy of Sciences`,category:`family`,tags:[`kids`,`science`,`aquarium`,`planetarium`,`rainy-day`],area:`Golden Gate Park`,lat:37.7699,lng:-122.4661,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`An aquarium, rainforest dome, planetarium and natural history museum under a living, planted roof.`,tip:`Book online to save; adults 21+ can come for Thursday NightLife evenings with music and drinks.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`California Academy of Sciences`},{id:`alcatraz`,name:`Alcatraz Island`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`history`,`prison`,`ferry`],area:`Alcatraz Island`,lat:37.827,lng:-122.423,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:47,rating:5,description:`The notorious former federal prison on "The Rock", brought to life by an excellent cellhouse audio tour narrated by ex-inmates and guards.`,tip:`Ferries leave from Pier 33 and sell out weeks ahead in summer; buy only from Alcatraz City Cruises. Night tours are extra atmospheric.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Alcatraz Island`},{id:`pier-39`,name:`Pier 39 & Sea Lions`,category:`family`,tags:[`free`,`kids`,`sea-lions`,`waterfront`],area:`Fisherman's Wharf`,lat:37.8087,lng:-122.4098,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Touristy but fun waterfront pier where hundreds of barking sea lions lounge on the floating docks.`,tip:`Skip the chain restaurants; walk to the Wharf's crab stands for sourdough bread bowls of clam chowder.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Pier 39`},{id:`cable-car-ride`,name:`Cable Car Ride`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`iconic`,`transport`,`history`,`hills`],area:`Union Square`,lat:37.785,lng:-122.4078,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:9,rating:4,description:`Clang up and over the city's steepest hills on the world's last manually operated cable car system.`,tip:`The Powell St turnaround line can take an hour; board a stop or two up the line, or ride the quieter California St line. Pay with Clipper or the MuniMobile app.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`San Francisco cable car system`},{id:`tonga-room`,name:`Tonga Room & Hurricane Bar`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`tiki`,`cocktails`,`kitsch`,`rainy-day`],area:`Nob Hill`,lat:37.7924,lng:-122.4102,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:3,description:`A gloriously over-the-top tiki bar in the Fairmont hotel, with a lagoon, a floating band barge and simulated tropical rainstorms.`,tip:`Opens in the evening Wednesday to Sunday; arrive early on weekends, when a cover charge may apply once the band starts.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Tonga Room`},{id:`chinatown`,name:`Chinatown`,category:`culture`,tags:[`free`,`walk`,`dim-sum`,`history`],area:`Chinatown`,lat:37.7908,lng:-122.4058,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`North America's oldest Chinatown, entered through the Dragon Gate, with lantern-strung Grant Avenue, temples and bustling Stockton St markets.`,tip:`Go in the morning for dim sum, and peek into the Golden Gate Fortune Cookie Factory on Ross Alley.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Chinatown, San Francisco`},{id:`city-lights-booksellers`,name:`City Lights Booksellers`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`books`,`beat-generation`,`history`,`rainy-day`],area:`North Beach`,lat:37.7976,lng:-122.4065,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The legendary Beat Generation bookshop and publisher founded in 1953, with a poetry room upstairs.`,tip:`Pair it with a drink at Vesuvio Cafe across Jack Kerouac Alley and an espresso in North Beach's Italian cafes.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`City Lights Bookstore`},{id:`coit-tower`,name:`Coit Tower`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`murals`,`walk`],area:`North Beach`,lat:37.8024,lng:-122.4058,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:3,description:`An Art Deco tower atop Telegraph Hill with Depression-era murals in the lobby and 360-degree views from the top.`,tip:`The lobby murals are free; walk up via the leafy Filbert Steps and listen for the wild parrots.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Coit Tower`},{id:`lombard-street`,name:`Lombard Street`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`free`,`photo`,`hills`],area:`Russian Hill`,lat:37.8021,lng:-122.4187,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The famous "crookedest street" zigzags through eight hairpin turns lined with hydrangeas.`,tip:`Walk down the stairs at the sides rather than queueing to drive; the Powell-Hyde cable car stops at the top.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Lombard Street (San Francisco)`},{id:`ferry-building`,name:`Ferry Building Marketplace`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`gourmet`,`waterfront`,`rainy-day`],area:`Embarcadero`,lat:37.7955,lng:-122.3937,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`A grand 1898 terminal reborn as a gourmet hall of oysters, cheese, coffee and bakeries on the bay.`,tip:`Come on Tuesday, Thursday or especially Saturday morning for the outdoor farmers market.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`San Francisco Ferry Building`},{id:`exploratorium`,name:`Exploratorium`,category:`family`,tags:[`kids`,`science`,`hands-on`,`rainy-day`],area:`Embarcadero`,lat:37.8017,lng:-122.3973,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:4,description:`Hundreds of hands-on science exhibits on Pier 15 that are just as fun for curious adults as for kids.`,tip:`Thursday-evening After Dark sessions are for ages 18+; the Tactile Dome needs a separate advance booking.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Exploratorium`},{id:`sfmoma`,name:`San Francisco Museum of Modern Art (SFMOMA)`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`modern-art`,`rainy-day`],area:`SoMa`,lat:37.7857,lng:-122.4011,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`Seven floors of modern and contemporary art, from Warhol and Rothko to Calder, plus a living wall and sculpture terraces.`,tip:`Closed Wednesdays; the ground-floor galleries are free to enter without a ticket.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`San Francisco Museum of Modern Art`},{id:`dolores-park`,name:`Mission Dolores Park`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`free`,`park`,`picnic`,`viewpoint`,`kids`],area:`Mission District`,lat:37.7596,lng:-122.4269,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The city's favourite sunny lawn, with skyline views and a lively weekend picnic scene.`,tip:`The Mission is often warm when the rest of town is foggy; grab supplies at Bi-Rite Market across the street.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Mission Dolores Park`},{id:`la-taqueria`,name:`La Taqueria`,category:`food`,tags:[`burrito`,`mexican`,`local-favourite`],area:`Mission District`,lat:37.7509,lng:-122.4181,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:4,description:`A no-frills Mission institution serving rice-free carnitas and carne asada burritos that defined the Mission style.`,tip:`Order it "dorado" for a griddle-crisped tortilla; cash and cards accepted but lines move fast.`,indoor:!0},{id:`twin-peaks`,name:`Twin Peaks`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`viewpoint`,`sunset`,`night-view`],area:`Twin Peaks`,lat:37.7544,lng:-122.4477,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Two grassy summits rising over 900 feet with a sweeping panorama from downtown to the Bay Bridge.`,tip:`Bring a warm jacket; it is windy and cold at the top, and best on a clear evening when the city lights come on.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Twin Peaks (San Francisco)`},{id:`muir-woods`,name:`Muir Woods National Monument`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`redwoods`,`hiking`],area:`Marin County`,lat:37.897,lng:-122.5811,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`A cathedral-like grove of old-growth coast redwoods, some over 1,000 years old, just 12 miles north of the Golden Gate.`,tip:`Parking or shuttle reservations are required in advance (go.muirwoods.org) on top of the $15 entry fee; there is no mobile signal on site.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Muir Woods National Monument`},{id:`palace-of-fine-arts`,name:`Palace of Fine Arts`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`free`,`architecture`,`photography`],area:`Marina District`,lat:37.8029,lng:-122.4484,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A dreamy Greco-Roman rotunda and colonnade reflected in a swan-filled lagoon, a surviving relic of the 1915 Panama-Pacific Exposition.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Palace of Fine Arts`},{id:`crissy-field`,name:`Crissy Field`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`beach`,`walking`,`bridge-views`],area:`Presidio`,lat:37.804,lng:-122.466,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A restored tidal marsh and bayfront promenade where the flat path leads towards the Golden Gate Bridge with kites, dogs and windsurfers all around.`,tip:`Walk west to Fort Point beneath the bridge, then refuel at the Warming Hut café.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Crissy Field`},{id:`haight-ashbury`,name:`Haight-Ashbury`,category:`culture`,tags:[`neighbourhood`,`vintage`,`music`,`history`],area:`Haight-Ashbury`,lat:37.7699,lng:-122.4469,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The cradle of 1967's Summer of Love, now lined with Victorian houses, vintage clothing shops, head shops and psychedelic murals.`,tip:`Amoeba Music at the park end of Haight Street is a giant of new and used vinyl.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Haight-Ashbury`},{id:`alamo-square`,name:`Alamo Square & the Painted Ladies`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`free`,`iconic`,`photography`,`skyline`],area:`Alamo Square`,lat:37.7764,lng:-122.4346,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A hilltop park facing the famous row of pastel Victorian houses with the downtown skyline rising behind them.`,tip:`Late afternoon puts the sun behind you for the classic postcard shot.`,indoor:!1},{id:`legion-of-honor`,name:`Legion of Honor`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`rodin`,`ocean-views`,`rainy-day`],area:`Outer Richmond`,lat:37.7845,lng:-122.5008,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:4,description:`A neoclassical palace on a cliff above the Golden Gate holding European old masters and one of the world's great Rodin collections.`,tip:`Your ticket also covers same-day general admission at the de Young in Golden Gate Park.`,indoor:!0},{id:`japanese-tea-garden`,name:`Japanese Tea Garden`,category:`nature`,tags:[`garden`,`tea`,`photography`,`peaceful`],area:`Golden Gate Park`,lat:37.7702,lng:-122.4704,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:13,rating:4,description:`The oldest public Japanese garden in the US, with a steep drum bridge, koi ponds, a pagoda and a tea house serving green tea and fortune cookies.`,tip:`Entry has traditionally been free on Monday, Wednesday and Friday mornings before 10 am; it gets crowded by midday.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Japanese Tea Garden (San Francisco)`},{id:`musee-mecanique`,name:`Musée Mécanique`,category:`family`,tags:[`arcade`,`vintage`,`kids`,`rainy-day`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Fisherman's Wharf`,lat:37.8094,lng:-122.4166,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:5,rating:4,description:`A free-entry hall crammed with antique coin-operated machines, from fortune tellers and player pianos to cranky mechanical dioramas, most still a quarter a play.`,tip:`Bring quarters (there are change machines) and say hello to the cackling Laffing Sal.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Musée Mécanique`},{id:`balmy-alley`,name:`Balmy Alley Murals`,category:`culture`,tags:[`free`,`street-art`,`murals`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Mission District`,lat:37.7523,lng:-122.4123,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A single Mission block where nearly every garage door and fence is covered in politically charged Latino murals, repainted since the 1970s.`,tip:`Combine with Clarion Alley near Valencia Street and a burrito at La Taqueria.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Balmy Alley`},{id:`castro`,name:`The Castro`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`lgbtq`,`bars`,`history`,`neighbourhood`],area:`Castro`,lat:37.7623,lng:-122.435,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The historic heart of LGBTQ+ San Francisco, with a giant rainbow flag, rainbow crosswalks, lively bars and the art-deco Castro Theatre marquee.`,tip:`The small GLBT Historical Society Museum on 18th Street adds great context.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Castro District, San Francisco`},{id:`sfjazz-center`,name:`SFJAZZ Center`,category:`culture`,tags:[`jazz`,`live-music`,`rainy-day`],area:`Hayes Valley`,lat:37.7764,lng:-122.4216,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:60,rating:4,description:`A purpose-built glass-walled jazz hall hosting everyone from legends to rising stars, with great sightlines from every seat.`,tip:`Spend the pre-show hour browsing the boutiques and beer garden of Hayes Valley.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`SFJAZZ Center`},{id:`kabuki-springs`,name:`Kabuki Springs & Spa`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`spa`,`baths`,`rainy-day`,`japantown`],area:`Japantown`,lat:37.785,lng:-122.432,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:60,rating:4,description:`Japanese-style communal baths with hot and cold plunges, a sauna and steam room, hidden in the Japantown complex.`,tip:`Communal bath days alternate between women-only, men-only and co-ed; check the schedule before you go.`,indoor:!0},{id:`sausalito`,name:`Sausalito by Ferry`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`ferry`,`cycling`,`bay-views`,`half-day`],area:`Marin County`,lat:37.8591,lng:-122.4853,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`A Mediterranean-style bayside town of houseboats, galleries and waterfront cafés, a scenic ferry ride from the city.`,tip:`Rent a bike, ride across the Golden Gate Bridge and down into Sausalito, then take the ferry back to the Ferry Building.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Sausalito, California`},{id:`napa-valley`,name:`Napa Valley Wine Country`,category:`food`,tags:[`day-trip`,`wine`,`tasting`,`scenic`],area:`Napa Valley`,lat:38.4013,lng:-122.3622,durationHours:9,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:150,rating:4,description:`America's most famous wine region, a valley of vineyards and grand tasting rooms with Yountville's acclaimed restaurants at its centre.`,tip:`Tastings at most wineries must be booked ahead and run $40–100 each; join a tour or pick a designated driver.`,indoor:!1},{id:`asian-art-museum`,name:`Asian Art Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`asia`,`rainy-day`],area:`Civic Center`,lat:37.7802,lng:-122.4161,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:4,description:`One of the largest collections of Asian art in the West, from Chinese jades and bronzes to Japanese screens, in the former main library opposite City Hall.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Asian Art Museum (San Francisco)`},{id:`baker-beach`,name:`Baker Beach`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`beach`,`sunset`,`bridge-views`],area:`Presidio`,lat:37.7936,lng:-122.4836,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A wild stretch of sand at the foot of the Presidio cliffs with a head-on view of the Golden Gate Bridge spanning the strait.`,tip:`The water is cold with strong currents, so it is for strolling, not swimming; the north end is clothing-optional.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Baker Beach`},{id:`ghirardelli-square`,name:`Ghirardelli Square`,category:`food`,tags:[`chocolate`,`dessert`,`kids`,`historic`],area:`Fisherman's Wharf`,lat:37.8059,lng:-122.4229,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`A red-brick former chocolate factory above the bay, now home to the original Ghirardelli soda fountain and its towering hot-fudge sundaes.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Ghirardelli Square`},{id:`the-fillmore`,name:`The Fillmore`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`live-music`,`historic`,`concerts`,`rainy-day`],area:`Fillmore District`,lat:37.784,lng:-122.433,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:60,rating:4,description:`The legendary rock ballroom where Bill Graham staged the Grateful Dead and Jimi Hendrix, still hosting touring bands under its chandeliers.`,tip:`At many sold-out shows, staff hand out free collectible concert posters on the way out.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`The Fillmore`},{id:`mission-dolores`,name:`Mission Dolores`,category:`culture`,tags:[`history`,`church`,`architecture`],area:`Mission District`,lat:37.7644,lng:-122.4269,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:7,rating:3,description:`The oldest intact building in San Francisco, a 1791 adobe mission chapel beside an ornate basilica and a small historic cemetery.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Mission San Francisco de Asís`}],foods:[{name:`Sourdough bread`,description:`Tangy, crusty loaves from the city's Gold Rush-era starter cultures, often served as a bread bowl of clam chowder.`},{name:`Mission burrito`,description:`An oversized foil-wrapped burrito stuffed with meat, rice, beans, salsa and more, born in the Mission District.`},{name:`Dungeness crab`,description:`Sweet local crab served cracked with butter or garlic, in season roughly November to June.`},{name:`Cioppino`,description:`A tomato-and-wine seafood stew created by Italian fishermen in North Beach.`},{name:`Dim sum`,description:`Steamed dumplings, buns and rolls from carts or counters in Chinatown and the Richmond District.`},{name:`Irish coffee at the Buena Vista`,description:`The bar near Fisherman's Wharf that popularised Irish coffee in the US still pours thousands a day.`}]},{id:`los-angeles`,name:`Los Angeles`,lat:34.05223,lng:-118.24368,timezone:`America/Los_Angeles`,tagline:`Beaches, movie magic and endless sunshine`,description:`A sprawling patchwork of beach towns, hillside canyons and film-industry neighbourhoods, from Hollywood and Downtown to Santa Monica and Venice. Distances are big and traffic is real, so plan each day around one or two areas; the weather is mild all year.`,idealDays:[3,5],places:[{id:`griffith-observatory`,name:`Griffith Observatory`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`free`,`viewpoint`,`sunset`,`science`],area:`Griffith Park`,lat:34.11833,lng:-118.30033,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`An Art Deco observatory on the slopes of Mount Hollywood with free telescopes, space exhibits and the best view of the Hollywood Sign and city lights.`,tip:`Come for sunset and stay after dark; parking fills fast, so take the DASH Observatory bus from Vermont/Sunset. Closed Mondays.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Griffith Observatory`},{id:`hollywood-sign`,name:`Hollywood Sign`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`free`,`hiking`,`viewpoint`,`photo`],area:`Hollywood Hills`,lat:34.13406,lng:-118.32159,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The giant white letters on Mount Lee are best seen from Lake Hollywood Park or on a hike up to the ridge behind them.`,tip:`You cannot touch the sign itself; the Brush Canyon or Mount Hollywood trails give close views. Start early to beat the heat.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Hollywood Sign`},{id:`hollywood-walk-of-fame`,name:`Hollywood Walk of Fame`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`free`,`walk`,`movies`,`photo`],area:`Hollywood`,lat:34.10166,lng:-118.34343,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`More than 2,700 brass-and-terrazzo stars line Hollywood Boulevard, honouring film, TV, music and radio legends.`,tip:`The busiest stretch is near Hollywood and Highland; it is gritty and touristy, so an hour is plenty.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Hollywood Walk of Fame`},{id:`tcl-chinese-theatre`,name:`TCL Chinese Theatre`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`movies`,`historic`,`architecture`,`photo`],area:`Hollywood`,lat:34.10194,lng:-118.34097,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The 1927 movie palace where stars leave hand- and footprints in the cement forecourt; it still hosts premieres and IMAX screenings.`,tip:`The forecourt is free to browse; catch an evening film in the huge IMAX auditorium for the full experience.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Grauman's Chinese Theatre`},{id:`universal-studios-hollywood`,name:`Universal Studios Hollywood`,category:`family`,tags:[`theme-park`,`kids`,`movies`,`rides`,`studio-tour`],area:`Universal City`,lat:34.13652,lng:-118.35605,durationHours:8,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:130,rating:5,description:`A working film studio and theme park, with the Studio Tour backlot tram, the Wizarding World of Harry Potter and Super Nintendo World.`,tip:`Do the Studio Tour early before queues build, and buy dated tickets online for a lower price.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Universal Studios Hollywood`},{id:`disneyland`,name:`Disneyland Park`,category:`family`,tags:[`theme-park`,`kids`,`rides`,`iconic`,`day-trip`],area:`Anaheim`,lat:33.8126,lng:-117.91897,durationHours:10,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:150,rating:5,description:`Walt Disney's original 1955 theme park in Anaheim, with Sleeping Beauty Castle, classic dark rides and evening fireworks and parades.`,tip:`Arrive before opening and use the Disneyland app for Lightning Lane; Disney California Adventure is right across the plaza.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Disneyland`},{id:`santa-monica-pier`,name:`Santa Monica Pier`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`beach`,`sunset`,`free`,`kids`],area:`Santa Monica`,lat:34.00861,lng:-118.49861,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A century-old pier with a solar-powered Ferris wheel, arcade, fishing spots and the symbolic end of Route 66 over a wide sandy beach.`,tip:`Free to walk; rides at Pacific Park are pay-per-ride. Stay for sunset, then walk the beach path south to Venice.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Santa Monica Pier`},{id:`venice-beach-boardwalk`,name:`Venice Beach Boardwalk`,category:`culture`,tags:[`beach`,`free`,`street-art`,`people-watching`,`skatepark`],area:`Venice`,lat:33.98671,lng:-118.4741,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A loud, colourful oceanfront promenade of street performers, murals, Muscle Beach, the skatepark and basketball courts.`,tip:`Rent a bike or e-bike and ride the Marvin Braude beach path between Venice and Santa Monica.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Venice Beach`},{id:`venice-canals`,name:`Venice Canals`,category:`culture`,tags:[`free`,`walk`,`architecture`,`quiet`,`photo`],area:`Venice`,lat:33.98361,lng:-118.46528,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A peaceful grid of canals, footbridges and eclectic homes, the surviving remnant of Abbot Kinney's 1905 "Venice of America".`,tip:`A few blocks from the boardwalk but far quieter; pair it with a stroll up Abbot Kinney Boulevard.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Venice Canal Historic District`},{id:`abbot-kinney-boulevard`,name:`Abbot Kinney Boulevard`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`boutiques`,`cafes`,`design`,`walk`],area:`Venice`,lat:33.9909,lng:-118.4666,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A tree-lined mile of independent boutiques, design shops, coffee bars and restaurants in the heart of Venice.`,tip:`Liveliest on weekend afternoons; walk it end to end from Venice Boulevard to Main Street.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Abbot Kinney Boulevard`},{id:`getty-center`,name:`Getty Center`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`architecture`,`gardens`,`viewpoint`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Brentwood`,lat:34.07796,lng:-118.47406,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`A hilltop campus of travertine pavilions holding European paintings, photography and decorative arts, with sweeping views and a sculpted Central Garden.`,tip:`Entry is free but parking costs about US$25; ride the tram up from the base and stay for late-afternoon light. Closed Mondays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Getty Center`},{id:`getty-villa`,name:`Getty Villa`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`antiquities`,`gardens`,`architecture`,`free`],area:`Pacific Palisades`,lat:34.04583,lng:-118.5645,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A re-created Roman country house above the Pacific, filled with Greek, Roman and Etruscan antiquities and formal gardens.`,tip:`Admission is free but a timed-entry reservation is required; check current opening days, which were reduced after the 2025 fires.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Getty Villa`},{id:`lacma`,name:`Los Angeles County Museum of Art (LACMA)`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`photo`,`rainy-day`,`iconic`],area:`Miracle Mile`,lat:34.0633,lng:-118.3592,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:28,rating:4,description:`The largest art museum in the western US, with collections spanning the globe and the much-photographed Urban Light installation of vintage street lamps.`,tip:`Urban Light is outdoors and free to see at any hour; it glows best after dusk. Closed Wednesdays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Los Angeles County Museum of Art`},{id:`la-brea-tar-pits`,name:`La Brea Tar Pits`,category:`museum`,tags:[`fossils`,`kids`,`science`,`park`],area:`Miracle Mile`,lat:34.0628,lng:-118.356,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:18,rating:3,description:`Bubbling asphalt seeps in Hancock Park that trapped Ice Age mammoths and sabre-toothed cats, with a museum of fossils and an active dig.`,tip:`The outdoor pits and Lake Pit are free to see; pay only for the museum and fossil lab.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`La Brea Tar Pits`},{id:`academy-museum`,name:`Academy Museum of Motion Pictures`,category:`museum`,tags:[`movies`,`design`,`viewpoint`,`rainy-day`],area:`Miracle Mile`,lat:34.06333,lng:-118.36083,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`The film academy's museum of movie history, costumes and props, with a glass-domed terrace looking up to the Hollywood Hills.`,tip:`Book timed tickets online; the Oscars Experience is an extra add-on worth it for film buffs.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Academy Museum of Motion Pictures`},{id:`the-broad`,name:`The Broad`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`contemporary`,`free`,`architecture`,`rainy-day`],area:`Downtown`,lat:34.0544,lng:-118.2506,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A honeycomb-clad museum of postwar and contemporary art, including works by Warhol, Koons and Basquiat, with free general admission.`,tip:`Reserve free timed tickets online; the Infinity Mirror Room needs a separate same-day sign-up. Closed Mondays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`The Broad`},{id:`walt-disney-concert-hall`,name:`Walt Disney Concert Hall`,category:`culture`,tags:[`architecture`,`music`,`free`,`iconic`],area:`Downtown`,lat:34.05528,lng:-118.25,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Frank Gehry's billowing stainless-steel concert hall, home of the LA Philharmonic, with a hidden rooftop garden open to the public.`,tip:`Free self-guided audio tours run on many mornings; for the full effect, book an evening LA Phil concert.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Walt Disney Concert Hall`},{id:`grand-central-market`,name:`Grand Central Market`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`street-food`,`historic`,`lunch`],area:`Downtown`,lat:34.05079,lng:-118.24885,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:15,rating:4,description:`A bustling food hall open since 1917, mixing old-school taco and produce stalls with newer favourites under one roof.`,tip:`Ride the tiny Angels Flight funicular across Hill Street up to Bunker Hill afterwards.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Grand Central Market`},{id:`olvera-street`,name:`Olvera Street`,category:`culture`,tags:[`historic`,`free`,`mexican`,`market`],area:`El Pueblo`,lat:34.0575,lng:-118.238,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A Mexican-style marketplace in the city's historic birthplace, with the 1818 Avila Adobe, craft stalls and taquitos.`,tip:`Visit the free Avila Adobe, the oldest standing house in LA, then cross to Union Station.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Olvera Street`},{id:`union-station`,name:`Union Station`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`architecture`,`historic`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Downtown`,lat:34.05515,lng:-118.23525,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A 1939 Mission Revival and Art Deco rail terminal with a grand waiting room of leather armchairs and tiled patios.`,tip:`Still a working hub for Metro and Amtrak, and a handy base to start a Downtown walk.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Los Angeles Union Station`},{id:`little-tokyo`,name:`Little Tokyo`,category:`culture`,tags:[`japanese`,`food`,`shopping`,`historic`,`free`],area:`Little Tokyo`,lat:34.05056,lng:-118.23944,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`One of the oldest Japantowns in the US, with ramen shops, mochi makers, a Buddhist temple and the Japanese American National Museum.`,tip:`Good for a cheap dinner of ramen or udon; the Japanese Village Plaza is the heart of the area.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Little Tokyo, Los Angeles`},{id:`the-last-bookstore`,name:`The Last Bookstore`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`books`,`free`,`photo`,`rainy-day`],area:`Downtown`,lat:34.04773,lng:-118.24982,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`California's largest new and used bookstore, set in a former bank with a famous tunnel built from stacked books upstairs.`,tip:`Free to browse; the upstairs book labyrinth and the vintage vault are the photo spots.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`The Last Bookstore`},{id:`huntington-library`,name:`The Huntington`,category:`nature`,tags:[`gardens`,`art`,`library`,`cactus`,`japanese-garden`],area:`San Marino`,lat:34.12722,lng:-118.11,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`A former estate with 130 acres of themed botanical gardens, a world-class library and art galleries including The Blue Boy.`,tip:`Book tickets ahead, especially at weekends; the Desert and Japanese gardens are the highlights. Closed Tuesdays.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Huntington Library`},{id:`runyon-canyon`,name:`Runyon Canyon Park`,category:`nature`,tags:[`hiking`,`free`,`viewpoint`,`dogs`],area:`Hollywood Hills`,lat:34.1093,lng:-118.3503,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A short, steep hike right above Hollywood, popular with locals and their dogs, with views from Downtown to the ocean on clear days.`,tip:`Enter from Fuller Avenue early in the morning; there is little shade, so bring water.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Runyon Canyon Park`},{id:`hollywood-bowl`,name:`Hollywood Bowl`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`music`,`concert`,`outdoor`,`picnic`,`iconic`],area:`Hollywood Hills`,lat:34.11278,lng:-118.33889,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:50,rating:4,description:`A legendary outdoor amphitheatre under its concentric arches, hosting LA Phil summer concerts, film-with-orchestra nights and big-name acts.`,tip:`The season runs roughly May to October; bring a picnic and wine, and take the Bowl Flyer shuttle instead of driving.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Hollywood Bowl`},{id:`rodeo-drive`,name:`Rodeo Drive`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`luxury`,`free`,`walk`,`iconic`],area:`Beverly Hills`,lat:34.06763,lng:-118.40135,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Three palm-lined blocks of flagship designer boutiques in Beverly Hills, made famous by countless films.`,tip:`Window-shopping is free; walk up the cobbled Via Rodeo and grab a photo by the Beverly Wilshire hotel.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Rodeo Drive`},{id:`original-farmers-market`,name:`Original Farmers Market & The Grove`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`food`,`shopping`,`historic`],area:`Fairfax`,lat:34.0725,lng:-118.36028,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:15,rating:3,description:`A 1934 market of food stalls, bakeries and old-fashioned grocers, next to The Grove open-air mall and its vintage trolley.`,tip:`Graze on stall food for lunch; LACMA and the Tar Pits are a short walk south.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Original Farmers Market`},{id:`california-science-center`,name:`California Science Center`,category:`family`,tags:[`kids`,`science`,`space`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Exposition Park`,lat:34.01556,lng:-118.28583,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A free hands-on science museum and home of Space Shuttle Endeavour, which from 13 November 2026 stands upright in launch position in the new Samuel Oschin Air and Space Center.`,tip:`General admission is free; Endeavour viewing needs a timed reservation, so book ahead once tickets open.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`California Science Center`},{id:`aquarium-of-the-pacific`,name:`Aquarium of the Pacific`,category:`family`,tags:[`kids`,`aquarium`,`sea-life`,`rainy-day`],area:`Long Beach`,lat:33.76216,lng:-118.19692,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`A big Long Beach aquarium of Pacific sea life, from sea otters and sharks to touch pools with rays and a walk-through lorikeet aviary.`,tip:`Reachable on the Metro A Line from Downtown; buy tickets online to save a little.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Aquarium of the Pacific`},{id:`point-dume`,name:`Point Dume`,category:`nature`,tags:[`beach`,`free`,`hiking`,`viewpoint`,`whale-watching`],area:`Malibu`,lat:34.00087,lng:-118.80684,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A rocky Malibu headland with a short bluff-top trail, sweeping Pacific views and sheltered coves below, on a drive along the Pacific Coast Highway.`,tip:`Look for migrating gray whales from December to April; parking is limited, so arrive early on weekends.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Point Dume`},{id:`sunset-strip`,name:`Sunset Strip`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`music`,`bars`,`clubs`,`rock`,`night`],area:`West Hollywood`,lat:34.09386,lng:-118.37677,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A mile and a half of Sunset Boulevard lined with rock clubs like the Whisky a Go Go and the Roxy, rooftop bars and giant billboards.`,tip:`Check club line-ups in advance; rideshare is easier than parking here at night.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Sunset Strip`},{id:`the-comedy-store`,name:`The Comedy Store`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`comedy`,`night`,`iconic`],area:`West Hollywood`,lat:34.0951,lng:-118.37384,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`A Sunset Strip stand-up club since 1972 where famous comics often drop in unannounced to test new material.`,tip:`Book ahead online; expect a drink minimum and a strict no-phones policy during shows.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`The Comedy Store`},{id:`warner-bros-studio-tour`,name:`Warner Bros. Studio Tour Hollywood`,category:`culture`,tags:[`movies`,`tv`,`studio-tour`,`behind-the-scenes`],area:`Burbank`,lat:34.15197,lng:-118.33661,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:75,rating:4,description:`A guided cart tour of working soundstages and backlot streets, ending with a museum of props, costumes and the Central Perk set.`,tip:`Book the first tour of the day; sets on the route change with whatever is filming.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Warner Bros. Studio Tour Hollywood`},{id:`echo-park-lake`,name:`Echo Park Lake`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`park`,`free`,`lake`,`paddle-boats`,`skyline`],area:`Echo Park`,lat:34.0725,lng:-118.26083,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A palm-fringed lake with lotus beds, swan pedal boats and Downtown skyline views, surrounded by a creative neighbourhood of cafes.`,tip:`Rent a swan boat on a sunny afternoon; the lotus flowers bloom in summer.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Echo Park Lake`},{id:`catalina-island`,name:`Catalina Island`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`island`,`ferry`,`snorkelling`,`day-trip`,`beach`],area:`Avalon`,lat:33.34308,lng:-118.32778,durationHours:8,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:85,rating:4,description:`A car-light island an hour offshore, with the harbour town of Avalon, clear water for snorkelling and kayaking, and wild hiking trails.`,tip:`Catalina Express ferries leave from Long Beach and San Pedro; take an early boat and rent a golf cart or bike in Avalon.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Santa Catalina Island (California)`}],foods:[{name:`Tacos al pastor`,description:`Spit-roasted, chilli-marinated pork shaved onto small corn tortillas with pineapple, onion and cilantro, sold from trucks and stands across the city.`},{name:`French dip sandwich`,description:`Thin-sliced roast beef on a soft French roll dipped in meat juices; two Downtown restaurants have claimed to invent it since 1908.`},{name:`Pastrami sandwich`,description:`Hand-cut, peppery smoked brisket on crusty rye bread, a classic of the city's long-standing Jewish delis.`},{name:`Korean barbecue`,description:`Marinated short ribs and pork belly grilled at the table with an array of banchan side dishes, a Koreatown tradition.`},{name:`Chili dog`,description:`A grilled hot dog smothered in meaty chilli, onions and cheese, served at roadside stands since the 1930s.`},{name:`California roll`,description:`An inside-out sushi roll of crab, avocado and cucumber, widely credited to sushi chefs in Los Angeles in the 1960s and 70s.`}]},{id:`las-vegas`,name:`Las Vegas`,lat:36.17497,lng:-115.13722,timezone:`America/Los_Angeles`,tagline:`Neon, big shows and red-rock desert on the doorstep`,description:`A desert city built for spectacle: the Strip's themed mega-resorts, dancing fountains and world-class shows, the vintage neon of Downtown's Fremont Street, and the futuristic Sphere. Beyond the lights, Red Rock Canyon, Hoover Dam and the fiery sandstone of Valley of Fire are all easy day trips.`,idealDays:[2,5],places:[{id:`las-vegas-strip`,name:`The Las Vegas Strip`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`free`,`iconic`,`walking`,`architecture`,`night-view`],area:`The Strip (Center)`,lat:36.1147,lng:-115.1728,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`Four miles of themed mega-resorts, from a replica Eiffel Tower and Venetian canals to Roman palaces, best walked as the neon flickers on.`,tip:`Distances are deceptive and summer heat is fierce; use the free trams between resorts and the air-conditioned walkways where you can.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Las Vegas Strip`},{id:`fountains-of-bellagio`,name:`Fountains of Bellagio`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`free`,`iconic`,`night-view`,`music`,`romantic`],area:`The Strip (Center)`,lat:36.11274,lng:-115.17428,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`More than a thousand water jets dance to music across the Bellagio's lake, soaring higher than the hotel's lower floors in a free show.`,tip:`Shows run every 15 minutes after dark; watch one from the street railing, then another from the Eiffel Tower deck opposite.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Fountains of Bellagio`},{id:`bellagio-conservatory`,name:`Bellagio Conservatory & Botanical Gardens`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`gardens`,`rainy-day`,`heat-escape`,`photo`],area:`The Strip (Center)`,lat:36.1133,lng:-115.1759,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A glass-roofed indoor garden restyled five times a year with tens of thousands of flowers and towering seasonal sculptures.`,tip:`Open around the clock and free; early morning is quiet, and the display changes every few months.`,indoor:!0},{id:`sphere`,name:`Sphere`,category:`culture`,tags:[`iconic`,`immersive`,`shows`,`rainy-day`,`heat-escape`,`night-view`],area:`The Strip (Venetian)`,lat:36.12073,lng:-115.16196,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:110,rating:5,description:`A 112-metre globe covered in LEDs outside and wrapped in a giant wraparound screen inside, showing immersive films such as The Wizard of Oz.`,tip:`Even without a ticket, the lit-up exterior is a free show after dark; the High Roller and Venetian walkways give good views.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Sphere (venue)`},{id:`fremont-street-experience`,name:`Fremont Street Experience`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`free`,`iconic`,`neon`,`light-show`,`live-music`,`night-view`],area:`Downtown (Fremont Street)`,lat:36.17067,lng:-115.14376,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Old Vegas under a vast LED canopy, where hourly light-and-music shows play above vintage casino signs, street performers and live bands.`,tip:`Canopy shows run on the hour from dusk; walk east afterwards to quieter Fremont East and the Container Park.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Fremont Street Experience`},{id:`high-roller`,name:`High Roller Observation Wheel`,category:`family`,tags:[`views`,`observation-wheel`,`night-view`,`kids`],area:`The Strip (LINQ Promenade)`,lat:36.11752,lng:-115.16815,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:4,description:`One of the world's tallest observation wheels, taking 30 minutes to turn in roomy glass cabins high above the Strip.`,tip:`Daytime tickets are cheaper, but a ride at dusk shows the Strip light up; it starts from the LINQ Promenade.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`High Roller (Ferris wheel)`},{id:`strat-skypod`,name:`The STRAT SkyPod`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`views`,`observation-deck`,`thrill-rides`,`night-view`,`rainy-day`],area:`North Strip (The STRAT)`,lat:36.14745,lng:-115.15556,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`The tallest freestanding observation tower in the US, with indoor and outdoor decks and hair-raising thrill rides hanging over the edge.`,tip:`Time it for sunset; the thrill rides and the SkyJump cost extra.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`The Strat`},{id:`eiffel-tower-viewing-deck`,name:`Eiffel Tower Viewing Deck`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`views`,`night-view`,`fountains`,`romantic`],area:`The Strip (Center)`,lat:36.11254,lng:-115.17228,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:3,description:`A half-scale Eiffel Tower at Paris Las Vegas, with an open-air deck that looks straight down on the Bellagio fountains.`,tip:`Go up after dark and wait for a fountain show below; lines are shortest on weeknights.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Paris Las Vegas`},{id:`welcome-to-las-vegas-sign`,name:`Welcome to Fabulous Las Vegas Sign`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`free`,`iconic`,`photo`,`retro`],area:`South Strip`,lat:36.08208,lng:-115.1728,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The famous 1959 diamond-shaped sign in the median of Las Vegas Boulevard, a must for the classic Vegas photo.`,tip:`Come early morning to avoid the queue; there is a small car park beside it, and buses on the Strip stop nearby.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Welcome to Fabulous Las Vegas sign`},{id:`neon-museum`,name:`Neon Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`neon`,`history`,`photo`,`night-view`,`iconic`],area:`Downtown (Las Vegas Blvd North)`,lat:36.17703,lng:-115.13527,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`A "boneyard" of giant retired signs from old casinos and motels, some restored to glow again, telling the city's story in neon.`,tip:`Book an evening slot to see the restored signs lit up; it is outdoors, so avoid summer midday.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Neon Museum`},{id:`mob-museum`,name:`The Mob Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`crime`,`interactive`,`rainy-day`,`heat-escape`],area:`Downtown (Fremont Street)`,lat:36.17278,lng:-115.14108,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`The National Museum of Organized Crime and Law Enforcement, set in a 1933 courthouse where real mob hearings were held.`,tip:`Allow more time than you think; the basement has a working distillery and a speakeasy bar.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Mob Museum`},{id:`grand-canal-shoppes`,name:`Grand Canal Shoppes & Venetian Gondolas`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`free`,`shopping`,`gondola`,`rainy-day`,`heat-escape`],area:`The Strip (Venetian)`,lat:36.12155,lng:-115.1695,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`An indoor Venice under a painted sky, with shops along a canal where singing gondoliers punt boats past St Mark's Square.`,tip:`Browsing is free; gondola rides cost extra and can be booked at the kiosk on the day.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Grand Canal Shoppes`},{id:`forum-shops`,name:`The Forum Shops at Caesars`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`free`,`shopping`,`luxury`,`rainy-day`,`heat-escape`],area:`The Strip (Caesars Palace)`,lat:36.1183,lng:-115.1759,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A lavish shopping arcade styled as an ancient Roman street, with fountains, statues and a sky that shifts from dawn to dusk.`,tip:`Enter from the Strip via the spiral escalator; it links straight into Caesars Palace.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`The Forum Shops at Caesars`},{id:`o-cirque-du-soleil`,name:`"O" by Cirque du Soleil`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`shows`,`acrobatics`,`iconic`,`rainy-day`],area:`The Strip (Center)`,lat:36.1124,lng:-115.1766,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:150,rating:4,description:`Cirque du Soleil's long-running water show at the Bellagio, where acrobats dive, swim and fly over a stage that turns into a pool.`,tip:`Usually two shows a night and dark on some weekdays; book ahead for good seats and avoid the splash rows if dressed up.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`O (Cirque du Soleil)`},{id:`wynn-lake-of-dreams`,name:`Lake of Dreams at Wynn`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`free`,`light-show`,`night-view`,`hidden-gem`],area:`North Strip (Wynn)`,lat:36.1269,lng:-115.1662,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A free after-dark show of projections, puppetry and music on a lake framed by a waterfall and forested mountain inside the Wynn.`,tip:`Shows run every half hour after dusk; watch from the free terrace viewing area rather than a lakeside restaurant.`,indoor:!1},{id:`flamingo-wildlife-habitat`,name:`Flamingo Wildlife Habitat`,category:`family`,tags:[`free`,`wildlife`,`flamingos`,`gardens`,`kids`],area:`The Strip (Center)`,lat:36.1162,lng:-115.1701,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A shady garden behind the Flamingo hotel where pink flamingos, pelicans, koi and turtles live among waterfalls and palms.`,tip:`Free and open in daylight hours; catch a feeding time in the morning.`,indoor:!1},{id:`shark-reef-aquarium`,name:`Shark Reef Aquarium`,category:`family`,tags:[`aquarium`,`sharks`,`kids`,`rainy-day`,`heat-escape`],area:`South Strip (Mandalay Bay)`,lat:36.0904,lng:-115.1768,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:3,description:`An aquarium at Mandalay Bay with a walk-through shark tunnel, a sunken-ship tank, rays and a touch pool.`,tip:`A good midday escape from the heat; the walk from the Mandalay Bay tram stop is short.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Shark Reef Aquarium`},{id:`big-apple-coaster`,name:`The Big Apple Coaster`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`thrill-rides`,`roller-coaster`,`views`],area:`South Strip`,lat:36.1024,lng:-115.1741,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:3,description:`A roller coaster that loops and barrel-rolls around the New York-New York skyline, with views over the south Strip.`,tip:`Ride after dark for the lights; loose items must go in lockers.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Big Apple Coaster`},{id:`area15-omega-mart`,name:`AREA15 & Omega Mart`,category:`family`,tags:[`immersive`,`art`,`kids`,`rainy-day`,`heat-escape`],area:`West of the Strip (AREA15)`,lat:36.13152,lng:-115.18128,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:55,rating:4,description:`A warehouse of immersive art, bars and games, home to Meow Wolf's Omega Mart, a surreal supermarket full of hidden doorways.`,tip:`Entry to the building is free; buy Omega Mart tickets ahead and give yourself at least two hours inside.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Area15`},{id:`arts-district`,name:`Arts District (18b)`,category:`culture`,tags:[`free`,`street-art`,`galleries`,`vintage`,`bars`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Downtown (Arts District)`,lat:36.1588,lng:-115.1529,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Local Las Vegas off the Strip: murals, galleries, vintage and antique shops, craft breweries and indie cafés around Main Street.`,tip:`Visit on the first Friday of the month for the street art festival, or browse the antique shops along Main Street.`,indoor:!1},{id:`springs-preserve`,name:`Springs Preserve`,category:`nature`,tags:[`gardens`,`desert`,`history`,`kids`,`trails`],area:`West Las Vegas (Springs Preserve)`,lat:36.167,lng:-115.1895,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:19,rating:3,description:`The site of the springs that founded Las Vegas, now desert gardens, trails, a small animal centre and the Nevada State Museum.`,tip:`Go in the morning before the heat; the Nevada State Museum on the grounds is included.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Springs Preserve`},{id:`atomic-museum`,name:`National Atomic Testing Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`science`,`cold-war`,`rainy-day`,`heat-escape`],area:`East of the Strip (Flamingo Road)`,lat:36.1142,lng:-115.1482,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:3,description:`The story of the Nevada Test Site, where nuclear bombs were tested just north of the city, told through artefacts and a simulated blast.`,tip:`A short ride east of the Strip; allow time for the Area 51 exhibit, which costs a little extra.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`National Atomic Testing Museum`},{id:`pinball-hall-of-fame`,name:`Pinball Hall of Fame`,category:`family`,tags:[`retro`,`games`,`cheap`,`rainy-day`,`hidden-gem`],area:`South Strip`,lat:36.0854,lng:-115.1716,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:3,description:`A hall packed with hundreds of playable pinball machines and arcade games from the 1950s on; entry is free and you pay per game.`,tip:`It is a short walk from the Welcome to Las Vegas sign; bring small bills or use the change machines.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Pinball Hall of Fame`},{id:`las-vegas-natural-history-museum`,name:`Las Vegas Science & Natural History Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`dinosaurs`,`kids`,`science`,`rainy-day`],area:`Downtown (Las Vegas Blvd North)`,lat:36.1818,lng:-115.1346,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:2,description:`A friendly family museum with roaring animatronic dinosaurs, a shark tank, African wildlife and an Egyptian tomb replica.`,tip:`Best for younger kids; it is a few minutes from the Neon Museum, so pair them up.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Las Vegas Natural History Museum`},{id:`discovery-childrens-museum`,name:`Discovery Children's Museum`,category:`family`,tags:[`kids`,`interactive`,`science`,`rainy-day`,`heat-escape`],area:`Downtown (Symphony Park)`,lat:36.1689,lng:-115.1533,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`Three floors of hands-on play and science exhibits around a giant climbing tower, aimed at children up to about 12.`,tip:`Closed some weekdays outside school holidays; check hours before you go.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Discovery Children's Museum`},{id:`smith-center`,name:`The Smith Center for the Performing Arts`,category:`culture`,tags:[`theatre`,`broadway`,`music`,`architecture`],area:`Downtown (Symphony Park)`,lat:36.1671,lng:-115.1528,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:80,rating:3,description:`Downtown's Art Deco-styled performing arts centre, hosting touring Broadway musicals, the Las Vegas Philharmonic and jazz nights.`,tip:`Check the programme before you travel; the intimate Myron's jazz cabaret is good value.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Smith Center for the Performing Arts`},{id:`downtown-container-park`,name:`Downtown Container Park`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`free`,`boutiques`,`kids`,`playground`,`quirky`],area:`Downtown (Fremont East)`,lat:36.1678,lng:-115.1388,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A small open-air mall built from shipping containers, with local boutiques, snack bars and a fire-breathing metal praying mantis at the gate.`,tip:`The mantis sculpture shoots flames after dark; the treehouse playground suits kids.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Downtown Container Park`},{id:`las-vegas-north-premium-outlets`,name:`Las Vegas North Premium Outlets`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`shopping`,`outlets`,`bargains`],area:`Downtown (Symphony Park)`,lat:36.1633,lng:-115.1566,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:2,description:`A large open-air outlet centre with well over a hundred designer and high-street brands at discount prices.`,tip:`Join the free VIP club online for an extra coupon book; go in the morning in summer as the walkways are outdoors.`,indoor:!1},{id:`chinatown-spring-mountain`,name:`Chinatown (Spring Mountain Road)`,category:`food`,tags:[`street-food`,`asian`,`late-night`,`local`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Chinatown (Spring Mountain Road)`,lat:36.1261,lng:-115.1973,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:4,description:`A long strip of plazas west of the Strip packed with pho shops, ramen bars, dim sum and dessert cafés, where locals actually eat.`,tip:`Many places stay open late; take a rideshare, as the plazas are spread over a few kilometres.`,indoor:!1},{id:`fly-linq-zipline`,name:`Fly LINQ Zipline`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`zipline`,`thrill`,`views`],area:`The Strip (LINQ Promenade)`,lat:36.1178,lng:-115.1703,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:2,description:`Ten parallel ziplines that launch from a tower and fly the length of the LINQ Promenade towards the High Roller.`,tip:`Ride side by side with friends; night rides above the lit promenade are the most fun.`,indoor:!1},{id:`red-rock-canyon`,name:`Red Rock Canyon National Conservation Area`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`hiking`,`scenic-drive`,`desert`,`iconic`],area:`Red Rock Canyon`,lat:36.1358,lng:-115.4277,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:5,description:`Towering red and cream sandstone cliffs half an hour from the Strip, with a 13-mile scenic drive and short hikes to rock scrambles and petroglyphs.`,tip:`Book a timed-entry reservation for the scenic drive in the cooler months, start early and carry plenty of water.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Red Rock Canyon National Conservation Area`},{id:`hoover-dam`,name:`Hoover Dam & Lake Mead`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`day-trip`,`engineering`,`iconic`,`views`,`history`],area:`Boulder City`,lat:36.01604,lng:-114.73775,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:5,description:`The colossal 1930s concrete dam on the Colorado River, with tours inside and the bridge high above, plus the blue waters of Lake Mead.`,tip:`Walk out on the Mike O'Callaghan-Pat Tillman bridge for the classic view; the guided tour adds the power plant.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Hoover Dam`},{id:`valley-of-fire`,name:`Valley of Fire State Park`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`hiking`,`desert`,`petroglyphs`,`photo`],area:`Valley of Fire (Overton)`,lat:36.4287,lng:-114.5138,durationHours:8,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:5,description:`Nevada's oldest state park, a maze of flaming red sandstone, swirling rock waves and ancient petroglyphs an hour from the city.`,tip:`Do the Fire Wave and White Domes trails early; some trails close in summer heat, and there is no food inside the park.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Valley of Fire State Park`}],foods:[{name:`All-you-can-eat buffet`,description:`The classic Vegas feast: lavish casino buffets with crab legs, carving stations and endless desserts.`},{name:`Prime rib`,description:`A thick slab of slow-roasted rib of beef with jus and horseradish, a Vegas steakhouse and casino-diner staple for decades.`},{name:`Steakhouse steak`,description:`Prime, dry-aged cuts seared hot and served with classic sides; Vegas has some of the country's grandest steakhouses.`},{name:`Shrimp cocktail`,description:`Chilled shrimp with tangy cocktail sauce, served in a tall glass, an old-school downtown casino favourite.`},{name:`Tacos al pastor`,description:`Spit-roasted, chilli-marinated pork shaved into small corn tortillas with onion, coriander and salsa, best from a Strip taquería late at night.`},{name:`Pho`,description:`Vietnamese beef noodle soup with a fragrant broth, the go-to late-night bowl in Chinatown.`}]},{id:`chicago`,name:`Chicago`,lat:41.87811,lng:-87.6298,timezone:`America/Chicago`,tagline:`Skyscrapers, lakefront beaches, blues and deep-dish`,description:`The birthplace of the skyscraper rises along Lake Michigan, with world-class museums in the Loop and on Museum Campus, a free lakefront trail and beaches, and lively neighbourhoods from Lincoln Park to Pilsen. Evenings mean blues clubs, jazz and improv comedy; summers are glorious, winters bitterly cold, so lean on the museums from November to March.`,idealDays:[3,5],places:[{id:`millennium-park-cloud-gate`,name:`Millennium Park and Cloud Gate`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`free`,`public-art`,`photo`,`park`],area:`The Loop`,lat:41.8827,lng:-87.6233,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`Anish Kapoor's mirrored "Bean" reflects the skyline in the city's showpiece park, alongside the Crown Fountain's spitting faces, the Lurie Garden and Frank Gehry's Pritzker Pavilion.`,tip:`Come early morning for a crowd-free photo with the Bean; in summer the Pritzker Pavilion hosts free evening concerts on the lawn.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Millennium Park`},{id:`art-institute-of-chicago`,name:`Art Institute of Chicago`,category:`museum`,tags:[`iconic`,`art`,`rainy-day`,`impressionism`],area:`The Loop`,lat:41.87963,lng:-87.62372,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:32,rating:5,description:`One of the world's great art museums, home to Seurat's A Sunday on La Grande Jatte, Hopper's Nighthawks, Grant Wood's American Gothic and a superb Impressionist collection.`,tip:`Buy timed tickets online; head straight upstairs to the Impressionists before the crowds, and note it is closed Tuesdays and Wednesdays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Art Institute of Chicago`},{id:`architecture-river-cruise`,name:`Chicago Architecture Center River Cruise`,category:`culture`,tags:[`iconic`,`architecture`,`boat`,`skyline`],area:`The Loop`,lat:41.8878,lng:-87.6242,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:57,rating:5,description:`A 90-minute boat ride along the Chicago River's three branches, with expert volunteer docents telling the story of more than 50 landmark towers.`,tip:`Departs from the dock at Michigan Avenue and Wacker Drive; runs roughly April to November, so book a day or two ahead in summer.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Chicago Architecture Center`},{id:`skydeck-willis-tower`,name:`Skydeck Chicago (Willis Tower)`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`viewpoint`,`night-view`,`rainy-day`],area:`The Loop`,lat:41.87885,lng:-87.63593,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:4,description:`The 103rd-floor observation deck of the city's tallest tower, where you can step out into The Ledge, glass boxes hanging 412 metres above the street.`,tip:`Go around sunset to see the city by day and night; on clear days you can see four states. Entrance is on Jackson Boulevard.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Willis Tower`},{id:`360-chicago`,name:`360 Chicago Observation Deck`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`night-view`,`lake-views`,`rainy-day`],area:`Streeterville`,lat:41.89887,lng:-87.62293,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:32,rating:4,description:`The 94th-floor deck of the former John Hancock Center looks straight down the Magnificent Mile and out over the lakefront beaches, with the tilting TILT windows for thrill-seekers.`,tip:`Skip the ticket and get a drink at the bar on the floors above for a similar view after dark; TILT costs extra.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`John Hancock Center`},{id:`chicago-riverwalk`,name:`Chicago Riverwalk`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`free`,`walk`,`architecture`,`night-view`,`drinks`],area:`The Loop`,lat:41.8879,lng:-87.6286,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A promenade along the south bank of the river, lined with wine bars, kayak rentals and terraced seating beneath the lit-up towers and bascule bridges.`,tip:`Stroll from Lake Shore Drive west to Lake Street at dusk; the cafes and bars mostly open from May to October.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Chicago Riverwalk`},{id:`magnificent-mile`,name:`The Magnificent Mile`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`shopping`,`architecture`,`walk`,`free`],area:`Streeterville`,lat:41.8948,lng:-87.6242,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Michigan Avenue's grand shopping strip runs from the Gothic Tribune Tower and Wrigley Building past flagship stores to the historic Water Tower.`,tip:`Start at the DuSable Bridge and walk north; the 1869 Water Tower, one of the few survivors of the Great Fire, is free to pop into.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Magnificent Mile`},{id:`navy-pier`,name:`Navy Pier`,category:`family`,tags:[`kids`,`lake-views`,`ferris-wheel`,`free`],area:`Streeterville`,lat:41.8918,lng:-87.606,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A kilometre-long pier jutting into Lake Michigan with the Centennial Wheel, boat tours, a children's museum and summer fireworks over the water.`,tip:`Entry is free but the wheel and rides cost extra; walk to the far end for the best skyline view.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Navy Pier`},{id:`field-museum`,name:`Field Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`dinosaurs`,`kids`,`rainy-day`,`natural-history`],area:`Museum Campus`,lat:41.86631,lng:-87.617,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:5,description:`A grand natural history museum starring SUE, one of the most complete T. rex skeletons ever found, plus Egyptian tombs and the man-eating lions of Tsavo.`,tip:`Basic admission covers most of the highlights; combine with the Shedd and Adler next door on one Museum Campus day.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Field Museum of Natural History`},{id:`shedd-aquarium`,name:`Shedd Aquarium`,category:`family`,tags:[`aquarium`,`kids`,`rainy-day`,`lake-views`],area:`Museum Campus`,lat:41.86763,lng:-87.61403,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`A Beaux-Arts aquarium with a Caribbean reef rotunda, Amazon rising flood forest and a glass-walled Oceanarium of beluga whales and dolphins framed by the lake.`,tip:`Book timed tickets online and arrive at opening; weekday mornings are much calmer than weekends.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Shedd Aquarium`},{id:`adler-planetarium`,name:`Adler Planetarium`,category:`museum`,tags:[`space`,`kids`,`rainy-day`,`skyline`],area:`Museum Campus`,lat:41.86633,lng:-87.6068,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:3,description:`America's first planetarium, with dome sky shows and space exhibits on a peninsula that also gives the classic postcard view of the downtown skyline.`,tip:`Even if you skip the museum, walk out along the path behind it for the best free skyline photo in the city.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Adler Planetarium`},{id:`buckingham-fountain`,name:`Buckingham Fountain`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`free`,`fountain`,`night-view`,`photo`],area:`Grant Park`,lat:41.8758,lng:-87.61893,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A huge rococo-style fountain in Grant Park, framed by the skyline, with water shows every hour and coloured lights after dusk.`,tip:`The fountain runs roughly May to mid-October; come after sunset for the light-and-water show.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Buckingham Fountain`},{id:`maggie-daley-park`,name:`Maggie Daley Park`,category:`family`,tags:[`kids`,`playground`,`free`,`ice-skating`],area:`Grant Park`,lat:41.8824,lng:-87.6192,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`An inventive park with a giant play garden, climbing walls and, in winter, a looping ice-skating ribbon winding through the trees.`,tip:`The playground is free; skate rental (winter) and the climbing wall cost extra.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Maggie Daley Park`},{id:`chicago-cultural-center`,name:`Chicago Cultural Center`,category:`culture`,tags:[`free`,`architecture`,`rainy-day`,`hidden-gem`],area:`The Loop`,lat:41.88372,lng:-87.62491,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The city's former central library, now a free arts centre, crowned by the world's largest Tiffany glass dome amid glittering mosaics and marble.`,tip:`Head to the third floor Preston Bradley Hall for the Tiffany dome; free exhibitions and lunchtime concerts run most days.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Chicago Cultural Center`},{id:`rookery-building`,name:`The Rookery`,category:`culture`,tags:[`architecture`,`hidden-gem`,`free`,`frank-lloyd-wright`],area:`The Loop`,lat:41.8788,lng:-87.6321,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`An 1888 office block by Burnham and Root whose light-filled atrium lobby was remodelled in white marble and gold by Frank Lloyd Wright.`,tip:`The lobby is free to peek into on weekdays; paid guided tours by the Frank Lloyd Wright Trust go upstairs.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Rookery Building`},{id:`buddy-guys-legends`,name:`Buddy Guy's Legends`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`blues`,`live-music`,`iconic`],area:`South Loop`,lat:41.87279,lng:-87.62611,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:4,description:`Blues legend Buddy Guy's own club, with live Chicago blues every night, guitars on the walls and Louisiana-style food.`,tip:`Free acoustic sets at dinner time on some days; the headline acts start later and carry a cover. Buddy himself plays a residency each January.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Buddy Guy's Legends`},{id:`kingston-mines`,name:`Kingston Mines`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`blues`,`live-music`,`late-night`],area:`Lincoln Park`,lat:41.9289,lng:-87.649,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:4,description:`Chicago's oldest and biggest blues club, open since 1968, with two stages trading sets back to back until the early hours.`,tip:`Music starts around 7:30 or 8pm and goes past midnight; one cover gets you both stages.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Kingston Mines (blues club)`},{id:`green-mill`,name:`Green Mill Cocktail Lounge`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`jazz`,`live-music`,`historic`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Uptown`,lat:41.96915,lng:-87.6598,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:15,rating:4,description:`A dim, velvet-boothed jazz lounge running since 1907, once a haunt of Al Capone, with live jazz most nights and the Uptown Poetry Slam on Sundays.`,tip:`Cover is cash only, and it fills up for weekend sets; arrive early for a booth and keep quiet during the music.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Green Mill Cocktail Lounge`},{id:`second-city`,name:`The Second City`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`comedy`,`improv`,`iconic`],area:`Old Town`,lat:41.9115,lng:-87.6348,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`The improv theatre that launched Bill Murray, Tina Fey and Stephen Colbert, still staging sharp sketch revues on its mainstage every night.`,tip:`Book ahead for the Mainstage revue; stay for the free improv set after the late show on many nights.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`The Second City`},{id:`wrigley-field`,name:`Wrigley Field`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`baseball`,`sport`,`iconic`,`historic`],area:`Wrigleyville`,lat:41.94838,lng:-87.65564,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`The ivy-walled 1914 home of the Chicago Cubs, where a day game with a hot dog in the bleachers is a classic Chicago ritual.`,tip:`The season runs April to September; outside it, take a ballpark tour. Ride the CTA Red Line to Addison, as parking is scarce.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Wrigley Field`},{id:`lincoln-park-zoo`,name:`Lincoln Park Zoo`,category:`family`,tags:[`zoo`,`kids`,`free`],area:`Lincoln Park`,lat:41.9211,lng:-87.6334,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`One of the oldest zoos in North America, free and open every day, with gorillas, polar bears and lions in a leafy park by the lake.`,tip:`Free entry, so it pairs easily with the conservatory next door; in winter evenings it hosts the ZooLights display.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Lincoln Park Zoo`},{id:`lincoln-park-conservatory`,name:`Lincoln Park Conservatory`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`greenhouse`,`rainy-day`,`garden`],area:`Lincoln Park`,lat:41.9245,lng:-87.6357,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A Victorian glasshouse of palms, ferns and orchids, a warm, green escape on cold days just north of the zoo.`,tip:`Free; check opening days before you go, as it closes on some weekdays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Lincoln Park Conservatory`},{id:`chicago-history-museum`,name:`Chicago History Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`rainy-day`,`great-fire`],area:`Lincoln Park`,lat:41.912,lng:-87.6317,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:22,rating:3,description:`The city's story from fur-trading post to the Great Fire of 1871, the World's Fair and the blues, told through engaging, hands-on galleries.`,tip:`Sits on the southern edge of Lincoln Park, an easy add-on to the zoo or an Old Town evening.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Chicago History Museum`},{id:`north-avenue-beach`,name:`North Avenue Beach and Lakefront Trail`,category:`nature`,tags:[`beach`,`free`,`cycling`,`skyline`,`summer`],area:`Lincoln Park`,lat:41.9117,lng:-87.626,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A sandy city beach with a ship-shaped beach house and skyline views, on the 29-kilometre Lakefront Trail that is perfect for a bike ride.`,tip:`Rent a Divvy bike and ride south along the trail to Museum Campus; lifeguards are on duty from late May to Labor Day.`,indoor:!1},{id:`garfield-park-conservatory`,name:`Garfield Park Conservatory`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`greenhouse`,`rainy-day`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Garfield Park`,lat:41.8864,lng:-87.7173,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`One of the largest conservatories in the US, with a primeval fern room, a desert house and Chihuly glass among the plants, all free.`,tip:`Take the Green Line to Conservatory-Central Park Drive, right outside; entry is free, with a suggested donation.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Garfield Park Conservatory`},{id:`national-museum-of-mexican-art`,name:`National Museum of Mexican Art`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`art`,`rainy-day`,`hidden-gem`,`murals`],area:`Pilsen`,lat:41.8561,lng:-87.6733,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A free museum of Mexican and Mexican-American art in the heart of Pilsen, famous for its Day of the Dead exhibition each autumn.`,tip:`Afterwards walk 18th Street to see Pilsen's colourful murals and grab tacos; closed Mondays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`National Museum of Mexican Art`},{id:`chinatown-chicago`,name:`Chinatown`,category:`food`,tags:[`food`,`culture`,`dim-sum`,`walk`],area:`Chinatown`,lat:41.853,lng:-87.6319,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`A compact Chinatown entered through its red gate on Wentworth Avenue, with dim sum halls, bakeries and Ping Tom Memorial Park on the river.`,tip:`Take the Red Line to Cermak-Chinatown; in summer the river water taxi links it with downtown.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Chinatown, Chicago`},{id:`the-606`,name:`The 606 (Bloomingdale Trail)`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`walk`,`cycling`,`local-life`],area:`Bucktown`,lat:41.914,lng:-87.6776,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A 4.3-kilometre elevated trail on an old rail line, gliding above Wicker Park, Bucktown and Humboldt Park past gardens and backyards.`,tip:`Hop off at Damen Avenue for the cafes and boutiques of Wicker Park and Bucktown.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Bloomingdale Trail`},{id:`griffin-museum-of-science-and-industry`,name:`Griffin Museum of Science and Industry`,category:`museum`,tags:[`science`,`kids`,`rainy-day`,`iconic`],area:`Hyde Park`,lat:41.79067,lng:-87.583,durationHours:3.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:27,rating:4,description:`A vast hands-on science museum in the last great building of the 1893 World's Fair, with a captured German U-boat, a replica coal mine and a 1930s streamliner train.`,tip:`Get there via the Metra Electric to 55th-56th-57th Street; the U-505 tour and coal mine ride cost extra and sell out on busy days.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Museum of Science and Industry (Chicago)`},{id:`robie-house`,name:`Frederick C. Robie House`,category:`culture`,tags:[`architecture`,`frank-lloyd-wright`,`unesco`,`tour`],area:`Hyde Park`,lat:41.78977,lng:-87.59597,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`Frank Lloyd Wright's masterpiece of the Prairie style, a long, low brick house on the University of Chicago campus listed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site.`,tip:`Visits are by guided tour only, so book a slot ahead; combine with the Museum of Science and Industry nearby.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Robie House`},{id:`promontory-point`,name:`Promontory Point`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`skyline`,`sunset`,`hidden-gem`,`lake-views`],area:`Hyde Park`,lat:41.7943,lng:-87.5799,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A man-made peninsula of limestone ledges jutting into the lake, loved by locals for swims, picnics and a sweeping view north to the skyline.`,tip:`A 10-minute walk from the Museum of Science and Industry; bring a picnic and stay for the skyline lights at dusk.`,indoor:!1},{id:`frank-lloyd-wright-home-and-studio`,name:`Frank Lloyd Wright Home and Studio`,category:`culture`,tags:[`architecture`,`frank-lloyd-wright`,`tour`,`suburb`],area:`Oak Park`,lat:41.8942,lng:-87.7997,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`The architect's own house and studio in leafy Oak Park, where he developed the Prairie style; the surrounding streets hold dozens of his homes.`,tip:`Ride the Green Line to Oak Park; book the guided interior tour, then walk the neighbourhood to see more Wright houses and Unity Temple.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Frank Lloyd Wright Home and Studio`},{id:`indiana-dunes`,name:`Indiana Dunes National Park`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`beach`,`hiking`,`dunes`,`summer`],area:`Indiana Dunes`,lat:41.658,lng:-87.063,durationHours:7,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:4,description:`Towering sand dunes, wild beaches and woodland trails along Lake Michigan's southern shore, with the Chicago skyline on the horizon.`,tip:`The South Shore Line train from Millennium Station reaches Dune Park and Beverly Shores; climb the 3 Dune Challenge for the best views.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Indiana Dunes National Park`},{id:`starved-rock`,name:`Starved Rock State Park`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`hiking`,`canyons`,`waterfalls`,`free`],area:`Starved Rock`,lat:41.3197,lng:-88.9944,durationHours:8,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Sandstone canyons and seasonal waterfalls along the Illinois River, with trails to bluff-top lookouts about two hours' drive southwest of the city.`,tip:`You need a car; waterfalls flow best in spring or after rain, and in winter the frozen falls draw ice climbers.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Starved Rock State Park`}],foods:[{name:`Deep-dish pizza`,description:`A tall, buttery crust baked in a pan and layered with cheese, fillings and chunky tomato sauce on top; it takes up to 45 minutes to bake.`},{name:`Italian beef sandwich`,description:`Thin-sliced, garlicky roast beef piled into a long roll, dunked in its juices and topped with sweet peppers or spicy giardiniera.`},{name:`Chicago-style hot dog`,description:`An all-beef frank on a poppy-seed bun "dragged through the garden" with mustard, neon relish, onion, tomato, pickle spear, sport peppers and celery salt; never ketchup.`},{name:`Tavern-style thin-crust pizza`,description:`The pizza locals actually eat most: a cracker-thin crust cut into squares, a bar-room staple since the 1940s.`},{name:`Maxwell Street Polish`,description:`A grilled Polish sausage with heaps of grilled onions, yellow mustard and sport peppers, born at the old Maxwell Street market.`},{name:`Jibarito`,description:`A Puerto Rican-Chicagoan sandwich invented in Humboldt Park, using flattened fried plantains instead of bread around steak, lettuce, tomato and garlic mayo.`}]},{id:`washington-dc`,name:`Washington, D.C.`,lat:38.9072,lng:-77.03687,timezone:`America/New_York`,tagline:`Marble monuments, free museums and the seat of power`,description:`The US capital is laid out around the National Mall, a two-mile lawn lined with memorials and the free Smithsonian museums, with the Capitol at one end and the Lincoln Memorial at the other. Beyond it lie brick-lined Georgetown, the U Street music scene and the revived waterfront; spring brings the cherry blossoms, summer is hot and humid.`,idealDays:[3,5],places:[{id:`lincoln-memorial`,name:`Lincoln Memorial`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`free`,`night-view`,`monument`,`history`],area:`National Mall`,lat:38.88929,lng:-77.05015,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`A Greek-temple memorial sheltering the giant seated Abraham Lincoln, looking down the Reflecting Pool to the Washington Monument and the Capitol.`,tip:`Open 24 hours; it is most moving after dark when lit up and quiet. Find the marker on the steps where Martin Luther King Jr. gave his "I Have a Dream" speech.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Lincoln Memorial`},{id:`washington-monument`,name:`Washington Monument`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`viewpoint`,`monument`,`free`],area:`National Mall`,lat:38.88948,lng:-77.03528,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:1,rating:4,description:`The 169-metre marble obelisk at the heart of the Mall, with an elevator to a viewing level that looks out over the whole city.`,tip:`Timed tickets are required: reserve on Recreation.gov up to 30 days ahead ($1 fee) or queue at the Monument Lodge on 15th Street from 8:45am for free same-day tickets.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Washington Monument`},{id:`jefferson-memorial`,name:`Thomas Jefferson Memorial`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`free`,`night-view`,`monument`,`reflection`],area:`Tidal Basin`,lat:38.8814,lng:-77.0365,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A domed, Pantheon-like rotunda on the Tidal Basin with a bronze Jefferson inside, glowing beautifully on the water at night.`,tip:`Part of an evening monuments loop: walk the Tidal Basin path here from the MLK and FDR memorials after dark.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Jefferson Memorial`},{id:`world-war-ii-memorial`,name:`National World War II Memorial`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`free`,`monument`,`fountain`,`night-view`],area:`National Mall`,lat:38.8894,lng:-77.0405,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A ring of 56 granite pillars and two triumphal arches around a fountain pool, honouring the 16 million Americans who served in World War II.`,tip:`It sits midway between the Washington Monument and the Lincoln Memorial, so fold it into a walk along the Mall.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`World War II Memorial`},{id:`vietnam-veterans-memorial`,name:`Vietnam Veterans Memorial`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`free`,`monument`,`history`,`moving`],area:`National Mall`,lat:38.8913,lng:-77.0477,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Maya Lin's black granite wall, cut into the earth and engraved with more than 58,000 names, is one of the most powerful memorials in the country.`,tip:`Directories at each end help you look up a name; visitors often make pencil rubbings with paper left by the rangers.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Vietnam Veterans Memorial`},{id:`tidal-basin-mlk-memorial`,name:`Tidal Basin and Martin Luther King Jr. Memorial`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`cherry-blossoms`,`walk`,`monument`],area:`Tidal Basin`,lat:38.8862,lng:-77.0442,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A loop around the Tidal Basin passes the towering Stone of Hope carving of Dr King and the open-air rooms of the FDR Memorial, ringed by the famous cherry trees.`,tip:`Peak bloom is usually late March to early April; the seawall was rebuilt in 2025 and young trees replanted, so some new stretches look sparse.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Tidal Basin`},{id:`white-house`,name:`The White House`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`free`,`photo`,`politics`],area:`Downtown`,lat:38.89768,lng:-77.03655,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The President's home, seen through the fence from Lafayette Square on the north side or across the Ellipse to the south.`,tip:`Inside tours must be requested through a member of Congress (US citizens) or your embassy, months ahead; security closures happen at short notice.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`White House`},{id:`united-states-capitol`,name:`United States Capitol`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`free`,`tour`,`politics`,`rainy-day`],area:`Capitol Hill`,lat:38.8899,lng:-77.0091,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`The domed home of Congress, toured from the underground Visitor Center through the Crypt and the Rotunda with its frescoed ceiling.`,tip:`Book a free tour online in advance (Monday to Saturday); no food or liquids are allowed through security.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`United States Capitol`},{id:`library-of-congress`,name:`Library of Congress (Thomas Jefferson Building)`,category:`culture`,tags:[`free`,`architecture`,`rainy-day`,`iconic`],area:`Capitol Hill`,lat:38.8887,lng:-77.0047,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`The world's largest library in a breathtaking 1897 building of marble, mosaics and murals, with a balcony view over the domed Main Reading Room.`,tip:`Free timed-entry passes are required: book online up to 30 days ahead, with same-day passes released at 9am. Open Tuesday to Saturday.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Thomas Jefferson Building`},{id:`national-archives`,name:`National Archives Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`history`,`rainy-day`,`documents`],area:`National Mall`,lat:38.89275,lng:-77.02304,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The original Declaration of Independence, Constitution and Bill of Rights, displayed in a dim, hushed rotunda.`,tip:`Entry is free; in busy seasons reserve a timed entry online to skip the line on Constitution Avenue.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`National Archives Building`},{id:`national-air-and-space-museum`,name:`National Air and Space Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`smithsonian`,`kids`,`rainy-day`,`iconic`],area:`National Mall`,lat:38.88816,lng:-77.01987,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`The Wright Flyer, Lindbergh's Spirit of St. Louis and the Apollo 11 command module in the Smithsonian's newly renovated flagship on the Mall.`,tip:`Free, but timed-entry passes are required for everyone; reserve on the museum website as soon as your date opens.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`National Air and Space Museum`},{id:`national-museum-of-natural-history`,name:`National Museum of Natural History`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`smithsonian`,`kids`,`rainy-day`,`dinosaurs`],area:`National Mall`,lat:38.8913,lng:-77.0261,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`A free Smithsonian giant with the cursed Hope Diamond, a vast fossil hall with a T. rex and a life-size North Atlantic right whale.`,tip:`No passes needed; enter from Constitution Avenue to dodge the Mall-side queue at peak times.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`National Museum of Natural History`},{id:`national-museum-of-american-history`,name:`National Museum of American History`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`smithsonian`,`rainy-day`,`history`],area:`National Mall`,lat:38.8912,lng:-77.03,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The Star-Spangled Banner that inspired the anthem, Dorothy's ruby slippers, Julia Child's kitchen and the First Ladies' gowns.`,tip:`Free with no passes; start with the flag on the second floor before the school groups arrive.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`National Museum of American History`},{id:`nmaahc`,name:`National Museum of African American History and Culture`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`smithsonian`,`rainy-day`,`history`,`iconic`],area:`National Mall`,lat:38.8911,lng:-77.0327,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`A bronze-latticed museum telling African American history from slavery to the present, starting deep underground and rising toward the light.`,tip:`Free; book timed passes online ahead for weekends and holidays. Allow time for the lower history galleries, which take hours.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`National Museum of African American History and Culture`},{id:`national-gallery-of-art`,name:`National Gallery of Art`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`art`,`rainy-day`,`sculpture-garden`],area:`National Mall`,lat:38.8913,lng:-77.0199,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`Free world-class art, including the only Leonardo da Vinci painting in the Americas, Vermeers and Impressionists, plus I. M. Pei's modern East Building.`,tip:`Walk the underground concourse with its light-art tunnel between the West and East buildings; the Sculpture Garden is next door.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`National Gallery of Art`},{id:`smithsonian-american-art-portrait-gallery`,name:`Smithsonian American Art Museum and National Portrait Gallery`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`smithsonian`,`art`,`rainy-day`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Penn Quarter`,lat:38.8978,lng:-77.0229,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Two free Smithsonian museums sharing a grand Greek Revival building, with the presidential portraits, American art and a glass-roofed courtyard.`,tip:`Open later than the Mall museums (until 7pm), so it is a good end to the day before dinner in Penn Quarter.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Old Patent Office Building`},{id:`hirshhorn-museum`,name:`Hirshhorn Museum and Sculpture Garden`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`smithsonian`,`modern-art`,`rainy-day`],area:`National Mall`,lat:38.8881,lng:-77.023,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The Smithsonian's modern and contemporary art museum, a concrete drum on the Mall with a sunken sculpture garden of Rodin and Moore bronzes.`,tip:`Free; the plaza fountain and sculpture garden across Jefferson Drive are lovely for a break between Mall museums.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Hirshhorn Museum and Sculpture Garden`},{id:`holocaust-memorial-museum`,name:`United States Holocaust Memorial Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`history`,`rainy-day`,`moving`],area:`National Mall`,lat:38.8867,lng:-77.0327,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`A profound, carefully told history of the Holocaust, with a permanent exhibition that follows the life of a real person through an identity card.`,tip:`Free timed passes are needed for the permanent exhibition from March to August; book online. Not recommended for children under 11.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`United States Holocaust Memorial Museum`},{id:`us-botanic-garden`,name:`United States Botanic Garden`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`greenhouse`,`rainy-day`,`garden`],area:`Capitol Hill`,lat:38.888,lng:-77.013,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A free glass conservatory at the foot of Capitol Hill, with a misty jungle room, orchids, desert plants and a lovely outdoor garden.`,tip:`Climb to the jungle canopy walkway; in December the holiday show recreates DC landmarks from plant materials.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`United States Botanic Garden`},{id:`international-spy-museum`,name:`International Spy Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`kids`,`rainy-day`,`interactive`,`espionage`],area:`L'Enfant Plaza`,lat:38.8842,lng:-77.0256,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:33,rating:4,description:`A playful, gadget-packed museum of espionage in which you take on an undercover identity and test your spy skills through interactive missions.`,tip:`Book a timed ticket online, which is usually cheaper than at the door; it is a short walk south of the Mall.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`International Spy Museum`},{id:`the-wharf`,name:`The Wharf`,category:`food`,tags:[`waterfront`,`free`,`night-view`,`dining`,`fish-market`],area:`Southwest Waterfront`,lat:38.879,lng:-77.0232,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A lively waterfront district of piers, restaurants and music venues, beside the Municipal Fish Market, the oldest continuously operating open-air fish market in the US.`,tip:`Grab steamed crabs or a fried fish sandwich at the fish market, then catch the free Wharf Jitney or water taxi.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`The Wharf (Washington, D.C.)`},{id:`arlington-national-cemetery`,name:`Arlington National Cemetery`,category:`culture`,tags:[`free`,`history`,`ceremony`,`moving`],area:`Arlington, Virginia`,lat:38.8801,lng:-77.0686,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`Rolling hills of white headstones across the Potomac, with the Kennedy graves, Arlington House and the precise Changing of the Guard at the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier.`,tip:`Take the Metro Blue Line to Arlington Cemetery; the guard changes every half hour in summer and hourly from October to March. A paid tram saves the hills.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Arlington National Cemetery`},{id:`georgetown`,name:`Georgetown`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`shopping`,`historic`,`walk`,`waterfront`,`dining`],area:`Georgetown`,lat:38.905,lng:-77.0627,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The city's oldest neighbourhood, with Federal-style brick rowhouses, boutiques on M Street, the C&O Canal towpath and a riverside park.`,tip:`There is no Metro stop, so walk 15 minutes from Foggy Bottom station; end at Georgetown Waterfront Park for sunset on the Potomac.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Georgetown (Washington, D.C.)`},{id:`dumbarton-oaks`,name:`Dumbarton Oaks Garden`,category:`nature`,tags:[`garden`,`hidden-gem`,`historic`,`flowers`],area:`Georgetown`,lat:38.9146,lng:-77.0632,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:11,rating:4,description:`Terraced formal gardens tumbling down a Georgetown hillside, with rose gardens, pools and orchards designed by Beatrix Farrand.`,tip:`Closed Mondays; a modest garden fee applies mid-March to October and it is free in winter. The small museum of Byzantine and pre-Columbian art is free.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Dumbarton Oaks`},{id:`blues-alley`,name:`Blues Alley`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`jazz`,`live-music`,`historic`,`dinner`],area:`Georgetown`,lat:38.9043,lng:-77.0626,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`The country's oldest continuously operating jazz supper club, an intimate brick carriage house in a Georgetown alley that has hosted Dizzy Gillespie and Wynton Marsalis.`,tip:`Buy tickets online; seating is first come, first served, so arrive early for the 8pm set. There is a food and drink minimum per person.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Blues Alley`},{id:`dc-improv`,name:`DC Improv`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`comedy`,`stand-up`],area:`Dupont Circle`,lat:38.9053,lng:-77.0407,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:3,description:`A basement comedy club on Connecticut Avenue that has booked touring headliners and rising stand-ups since the early 1990s.`,tip:`Book ahead for weekend headliners; a two-item food or drink minimum usually applies on top of the ticket.`,indoor:!0},{id:`u-street`,name:`U Street Corridor`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`live-music`,`bars`,`history`,`murals`],area:`U Street`,lat:38.917,lng:-77.029,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`Once called Black Broadway, where Duke Ellington grew up, U Street is now the city's nightlife strip of live-music venues, rooftop bars and the historic Lincoln Theatre.`,tip:`Start with a half-smoke at Ben's Chili Bowl, then catch a gig at the 9:30 Club or the Howard Theatre nearby.`,indoor:!1},{id:`eastern-market`,name:`Eastern Market`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`food`,`local-life`,`flea-market`],area:`Capitol Hill`,lat:38.8866,lng:-76.9964,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`A red-brick 1873 public market hall of butchers, bakers and produce stalls, joined at weekends by an outdoor flea market and craft stalls.`,tip:`Go on Saturday or Sunday morning for the full scene; the market is closed Mondays. Eastern Market Metro is a block away.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Eastern Market, Washington, D.C.`},{id:`union-market`,name:`Union Market`,category:`food`,tags:[`food-hall`,`local-life`,`rainy-day`],area:`Union Market District`,lat:38.9083,lng:-76.9975,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`A buzzing food hall in a former wholesale market, packed with local vendors serving everything from oysters and tacos to Ethiopian coffee.`,tip:`Weekend afternoons are busiest; the surrounding warehouse district has plenty more restaurants and bars.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Union Market`},{id:`washington-national-cathedral`,name:`Washington National Cathedral`,category:`culture`,tags:[`architecture`,`gothic`,`rainy-day`,`viewpoint`],area:`Cathedral Heights`,lat:38.9307,lng:-77.0707,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`A soaring neo-Gothic cathedral built over 83 years, with dazzling stained glass, including a window holding a moon rock, and a Darth Vader gargoyle to spot.`,tip:`Bring binoculars for the gargoyles; the sightseeing fee is waived for services and prayer, and the Bishop's Garden is free.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Washington National Cathedral`},{id:`national-zoo`,name:`Smithsonian's National Zoo`,category:`family`,tags:[`zoo`,`free`,`kids`,`pandas`,`smithsonian`],area:`Woodley Park`,lat:38.9296,lng:-77.0498,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A free Smithsonian zoo set in Rock Creek Park, where giant pandas are back alongside elephants, great apes and big cats.`,tip:`Enter at the top from Connecticut Avenue (Woodley Park or Cleveland Park Metro) and walk downhill; parking costs extra.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`National Zoological Park (United States)`},{id:`theodore-roosevelt-island`,name:`Theodore Roosevelt Island`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`hiking`,`hidden-gem`,`wildlife`],area:`Arlington, Virginia`,lat:38.8969,lng:-77.0644,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A wooded island in the Potomac, reached by footbridge, with quiet trails through swamp and forest to a memorial plaza for the conservationist president.`,tip:`Reach the footbridge from the Mount Vernon Trail parking lot; it pairs with a kayak from the Georgetown waterfront.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Theodore Roosevelt Island`},{id:`udvar-hazy-center`,name:`Steven F. Udvar-Hazy Center`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`smithsonian`,`kids`,`rainy-day`,`aviation`],area:`Chantilly, Virginia`,lat:38.9111,lng:-77.4442,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Air and Space's giant hangars near Dulles Airport, home to the Space Shuttle Discovery, an SR-71 Blackbird and the Enola Gay.`,tip:`Free with no passes, but parking costs $15 per car; it is easiest by car or combined with a Dulles flight.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Steven F. Udvar-Hazy Center`},{id:`mount-vernon`,name:`George Washington's Mount Vernon`,category:`culture`,tags:[`day-trip`,`history`,`estate`,`gardens`,`river-views`],area:`Mount Vernon, Virginia`,lat:38.72972,lng:-77.1075,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`George Washington's Potomac River plantation, with a tour of the mansion, gardens, a working farm, his tomb and the stories of the people enslaved there.`,tip:`Book a timed mansion entry online; reach it by car, Fairfax Connector bus 101 from Huntington Metro, a seasonal boat from the Wharf, or bike the Mount Vernon Trail.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Mount Vernon`},{id:`old-town-alexandria`,name:`Old Town Alexandria`,category:`culture`,tags:[`historic`,`walk`,`waterfront`,`shopping`,`free`],area:`Alexandria, Virginia`,lat:38.8048,lng:-77.0425,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Cobbled streets and 18th-century townhouses running down King Street to a Potomac waterfront, home of the Torpedo Factory Art Center.`,tip:`Take the Metro to King St-Old Town, then the free King Street Trolley to the river; the Torpedo Factory artist studios are free to browse.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Old Town Alexandria`},{id:`annapolis`,name:`Annapolis`,category:`culture`,tags:[`day-trip`,`sailing`,`historic`,`seafood`,`waterfront`],area:`Annapolis`,lat:38.9774,lng:-76.4855,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:4,description:`Maryland's sailing-mad colonial capital on Chesapeake Bay, with a historic harbour, the 18th-century State House and the US Naval Academy.`,tip:`Visitors need ID to enter the Naval Academy grounds; stay for steamed blue crabs on the waterfront.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Annapolis, Maryland`}],foods:[{name:`Half-smoke`,description:`D.C.'s own sausage: a coarse, smoky, half-pork half-beef link, split, grilled and smothered in chili, mustard and onions.`},{name:`Maryland crab cake`,description:`Big lumps of sweet Chesapeake blue crab bound with as little filler as possible and seasoned with Old Bay, broiled or fried.`},{name:`Mumbo sauce wings`,description:`Fried chicken wings doused in mumbo (or mambo) sauce, a sweet, tangy, red-orange sauce sold at the city's carry-outs.`},{name:`Ethiopian injera platter`,description:`Spicy stews, lentils and greens spooned onto a sheet of spongy, sour injera bread, eaten with the hands; D.C. has one of the largest Ethiopian communities outside Africa.`},{name:`Jumbo slice`,description:`An enormous, floppy slice of cheese pizza, longer than a dinner plate, sold late at night in Adams Morgan.`},{name:`Chesapeake oysters`,description:`Briny, mild oysters from Chesapeake Bay and Virginia waters, shucked raw at raw bars across the city.`}]},{id:`boston`,name:`Boston`,lat:42.36008,lng:-71.05888,timezone:`America/New_York`,tagline:`Revolutionary history, brownstones, seafood and Fenway`,description:`America's story starts here: the red-brick Freedom Trail links the sites of the Revolution, from Boston Common through the Italian North End to Bunker Hill. Gas-lit Beacon Hill, the grand avenues of Back Bay, first-rate museums and Harvard across the river fill the rest of your days, with lobster rolls, chowder and oysters on every corner. Spring and autumn are glorious; winters are cold and snowy, so lean on the museums.`,idealDays:[3,5],places:[{id:`freedom-trail`,name:`The Freedom Trail`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`free`,`history`,`walk`,`revolution`],area:`Downtown`,lat:42.3556,lng:-71.0636,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`A 4-kilometre line of red bricks winding past 16 sites of the American Revolution, from Boston Common and the Old State House to Paul Revere's house and the Bunker Hill Monument.`,tip:`Start at the Boston Common visitor centre and walk north; the trail is free, and only a few stops charge small entry fees. Join a costumed guided tour for the first stretch if you like stories.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Freedom Trail`},{id:`boston-public-garden`,name:`Boston Public Garden`,category:`nature`,tags:[`iconic`,`free`,`garden`,`kids`,`photo`],area:`Back Bay`,lat:42.35411,lng:-71.07034,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`America's first public botanical garden, with weeping willows around a lagoon, the pedal-powered Swan Boats and the bronze ducklings from Make Way for Ducklings.`,tip:`The Swan Boats run from mid-April to around Labor Day; stroll on across Charles Street into Boston Common, the oldest city park in the country.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Boston Public Garden`},{id:`faneuil-hall-marketplace`,name:`Faneuil Hall and Quincy Market`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`iconic`,`history`,`food-hall`,`street-performers`,`free`],area:`Downtown`,lat:42.36003,lng:-71.05624,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The 1742 meeting hall known as the Cradle of Liberty, beside the long granite Quincy Market food hall and cobbled plazas full of street performers.`,tip:`Pop upstairs in Faneuil Hall to see the Great Hall where revolutionaries met; the food hall is touristy, so save serious meals for the North End nearby.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Faneuil Hall`},{id:`museum-of-fine-arts-boston`,name:`Museum of Fine Arts, Boston`,category:`museum`,tags:[`iconic`,`art`,`rainy-day`,`impressionism`],area:`Fenway`,lat:42.33938,lng:-71.09404,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:5,description:`One of America's great encyclopaedic museums, with a superb Art of the Americas wing, Monets and Van Goghs, Egyptian treasures and the John Singer Sargent rotunda murals.`,tip:`Buy timed tickets online and check the opening days before you go; the Art of the Americas wing alone deserves an hour.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Museum of Fine Arts, Boston`},{id:`isabella-stewart-gardner-museum`,name:`Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`rainy-day`,`courtyard`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Fenway`,lat:42.33819,lng:-71.09908,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`A Venetian-style palazzo arranged exactly as its eccentric founder left it, around a blooming glass-roofed courtyard, with empty frames still marking the art stolen in the famous 1990 heist.`,tip:`Closed Tuesdays; anyone named Isabella gets in free, as does everyone on their birthday. Book a timed ticket on weekends.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum`},{id:`fenway-park`,name:`Fenway Park`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`baseball`,`sport`,`historic`],area:`Fenway`,lat:42.34665,lng:-71.09722,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:5,description:`The oldest ballpark in Major League Baseball, home of the Red Sox since 1912, where the towering Green Monster looms over left field.`,tip:`The season runs April to September; outside it, or on non-game days, take the hour-long ballpark tour. Grab a sausage on Lansdowne Street before the game.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Fenway Park`},{id:`north-end-boston`,name:`The North End`,category:`food`,tags:[`food`,`italian`,`history`,`walk`,`cannoli`],area:`North End`,lat:42.3635,lng:-71.0544,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`Boston's oldest neighbourhood and its Little Italy, a warren of narrow streets packed with trattorias, espresso bars and pastry shops along Hanover Street.`,tip:`Come hungry in the evening, when the restaurants buzz; in summer weekends the streets fill with saints' feast processions.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`North End, Boston`},{id:`paul-revere-house`,name:`Paul Revere House`,category:`culture`,tags:[`history`,`revolution`,`freedom-trail`],area:`North End`,lat:42.36372,lng:-71.05369,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:3,description:`The timber-framed home of the patriot silversmith, built around 1680 and the oldest house in downtown Boston, from where Revere set off on his midnight ride.`,tip:`A quick, self-guided visit; combine with the Old North Church a few minutes' walk away.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Paul Revere House`},{id:`old-north-church`,name:`Old North Church`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`history`,`church`,`revolution`,`freedom-trail`],area:`North End`,lat:42.36632,lng:-71.05442,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:4,description:`Boston's oldest standing church, whose steeple held the two lanterns, "one if by land, two if by sea", that signalled the British march in 1775.`,tip:`Paid behind-the-scenes tours take you up into the bell chamber or down into the crypt; the box pews alone are worth a look.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Old North Church`},{id:`uss-constitution`,name:`USS Constitution`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`free`,`history`,`ship`,`kids`,`freedom-trail`],area:`Charlestown`,lat:42.37247,lng:-71.05652,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`"Old Ironsides", launched in 1797, is the oldest commissioned warship still afloat, crewed by active-duty US Navy sailors who lead free tours of her decks.`,tip:`Adults need photo ID for the security check; the museum next to the dock is free by donation. Opening days vary by season, so check before crossing the bridge.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`USS Constitution`},{id:`bunker-hill-monument`,name:`Bunker Hill Monument`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`free`,`history`,`viewpoint`,`freedom-trail`],area:`Charlestown`,lat:42.37632,lng:-71.06078,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A 67-metre granite obelisk marking the first major battle of the Revolution, with 294 steps up to views over the harbour and the city.`,tip:`The climb is free; it marks the end of the Freedom Trail, so take the ferry from the Navy Yard back to Long Wharf afterwards.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Bunker Hill Monument`},{id:`harvard-yard`,name:`Harvard Yard and Harvard Square`,category:`culture`,tags:[`free`,`university`,`history`,`walk`,`bookshops`],area:`Cambridge`,lat:42.37445,lng:-71.11683,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The leafy, red-brick heart of America's oldest university, founded in 1636, beside the bookshops, cafes and buskers of Harvard Square.`,tip:`Ride the Red Line to Harvard; student-led walking tours start nearby, and the Harvard Art Museums make a good rainy add-on.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Harvard Yard`},{id:`mit-museum`,name:`MIT Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`science`,`robots`,`rainy-day`,`kids`],area:`Cambridge`,lat:42.36231,lng:-71.08626,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`A playful museum of robots, holograms, kinetic sculpture and AI experiments in a modern building in Kendall Square, showing off the work of MIT's labs.`,tip:`Right outside the Kendall/MIT Red Line stop; walk on through the MIT campus to see the Great Dome and Frank Gehry's Stata Center.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`MIT Museum`},{id:`new-england-aquarium`,name:`New England Aquarium`,category:`family`,tags:[`aquarium`,`kids`,`rainy-day`,`waterfront`],area:`Waterfront`,lat:42.35905,lng:-71.04961,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:38,rating:4,description:`A harbourside aquarium built around a four-storey Giant Ocean Tank of sea turtles and sharks, with a colony of penguins at its base and harbour seals outside.`,tip:`Book a timed ticket online; it also runs seasonal whale-watching cruises from the wharf next door, roughly April to October.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`New England Aquarium`},{id:`boston-tea-party-ships`,name:`Boston Tea Party Ships & Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`kids`,`rainy-day`,`interactive`,`revolution`],area:`Seaport`,lat:42.35216,lng:-71.05124,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:36,rating:3,description:`A lively, actor-led museum on replica 18th-century ships where you join a 1773 town meeting and hurl tea chests into the harbour.`,tip:`Visits run as timed guided experiences, so book ahead; great for kids, while adults may find it theatrical.`,indoor:!0},{id:`institute-of-contemporary-art-boston`,name:`Institute of Contemporary Art`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`modern-architecture`,`rainy-day`,`waterfront`],area:`Seaport`,lat:42.3529,lng:-71.0431,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`A dramatic glass-and-steel building cantilevered over Boston Harbor, showing bold contemporary art with a harbour-view gallery and waterfront steps.`,tip:`Sit on the wooden grandstand steps outside at the water's edge; the Seaport's restaurants and Harborwalk are on the doorstep.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Institute of Contemporary Art, Boston`},{id:`view-boston`,name:`View Boston Observation Deck`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`night-view`,`rainy-day`,`sunset`],area:`Back Bay`,lat:42.3471,lng:-71.0825,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:4,description:`Three floors at the top of the Prudential Tower with 360-degree views over the Charles River, Back Bay brownstones and the harbour, plus an open-air terrace and bar.`,tip:`Time your visit for sunset to see the city by day and night; it stays open late in the evening.`,indoor:!0},{id:`museum-of-science-boston`,name:`Museum of Science`,category:`family`,tags:[`science`,`kids`,`rainy-day`,`planetarium`],area:`West End`,lat:42.36771,lng:-71.07109,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:33,rating:4,description:`A huge hands-on science museum straddling the Charles River dam, famous for its indoor lightning show from a giant Van de Graaff generator.`,tip:`The planetarium and Omni theatre cost extra; catch the Theater of Electricity show, which runs several times a day.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Museum of Science (Boston)`},{id:`boston-public-library-central`,name:`Boston Public Library, Central Library`,category:`culture`,tags:[`free`,`architecture`,`rainy-day`,`murals`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Back Bay`,lat:42.34937,lng:-71.07807,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A palace of a public library on Copley Square, with the barrel-vaulted Bates Hall reading room, Sargent murals and an arcaded Italianate courtyard.`,tip:`Free art and architecture tours run most days; across the square, H. H. Richardson's Trinity Church is a masterpiece in its own right.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Boston Central Library`},{id:`beacon-hill-acorn-street`,name:`Beacon Hill and Acorn Street`,category:`culture`,tags:[`free`,`architecture`,`photo`,`walk`,`iconic`],area:`Beacon Hill`,lat:42.35779,lng:-71.06967,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Gas lamps, brick sidewalks and Federal-style row houses climb the hill behind the State House, with cobbled Acorn Street among the most photographed lanes in America.`,tip:`Go early morning for Acorn Street without crowds, then browse the antique shops and cafes of Charles Street at the bottom of the hill.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Beacon Hill, Boston`},{id:`massachusetts-state-house`,name:`Massachusetts State House`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`free`,`architecture`,`history`,`freedom-trail`],area:`Beacon Hill`,lat:42.35873,lng:-71.06375,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Charles Bulfinch's 1798 capitol crowned by a gleaming gold dome, overlooking Boston Common from the top of Beacon Hill.`,tip:`Free guided tours run on weekdays; bring photo ID for the security check.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Massachusetts State House`},{id:`mapparium`,name:`Mapparium`,category:`museum`,tags:[`hidden-gem`,`rainy-day`,`quirky`,`maps`],area:`Back Bay`,lat:42.3447,lng:-71.0854,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:3,description:`A three-storey stained-glass globe from 1935 that you walk through on a glass bridge, showing the world's borders as they were then, with odd whispering-gallery acoustics.`,tip:`Inside the Mary Baker Eddy Library; visits are in small timed groups, so arrive a little early.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Mapparium`},{id:`newbury-street`,name:`Newbury Street`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`shopping`,`brownstones`,`cafes`,`walk`,`free`],area:`Back Bay`,lat:42.35052,lng:-71.07985,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Eight blocks of Victorian brownstones turned boutiques, galleries and cafes, running from the Public Garden to Massachusetts Avenue.`,tip:`Upscale shops cluster near the Public Garden end; it gets cheaper and quirkier towards Mass Ave. Some Sundays in summer it closes to cars.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Newbury Street`},{id:`charles-river-esplanade`,name:`Charles River Esplanade`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`free`,`walk`,`sunset`,`river`,`cycling`],area:`Back Bay`,lat:42.3574,lng:-71.0736,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A riverside park of lagoons, docks and paths along the Charles, where sailboats tack in front of the Cambridge skyline and the Hatch Shell hosts summer concerts.`,tip:`Walk west towards the Mass Ave bridge at sunset; in summer the Hatch Shell holds free movies and concerts.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Charles River Esplanade`},{id:`rose-kennedy-greenway`,name:`Rose Kennedy Greenway`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`free`,`park`,`kids`,`public-art`,`food-trucks`],area:`Downtown`,lat:42.358,lng:-71.053,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A ribbon of gardens, fountains and public art laid over the buried former highway, linking Chinatown, the Waterfront and the North End.`,tip:`Kids love the fountains and the carousel of local animals; food trucks gather near Dewey Square on weekdays in warmer months.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Rose Fitzgerald Kennedy Greenway`},{id:`boston-harbor-islands`,name:`Boston Harbor Islands (Georges Island)`,category:`nature`,tags:[`boat`,`history`,`fort`,`summer`,`kids`],area:`Boston Harbor`,lat:42.3194,lng:-70.9296,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:3,description:`A short ferry ride from Long Wharf to a harbour island crowned by Fort Warren, a granite Civil War fort with tunnels to explore and picnic lawns facing the skyline.`,tip:`Ferries run roughly May to mid-October; bring food and water, as island facilities are basic.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Boston Harbor Islands National and State Park`},{id:`castle-island`,name:`Castle Island and Fort Independence`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`walk`,`harbour-views`,`local-life`,`hidden-gem`],area:`South Boston`,lat:42.3379,lng:-71.0125,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A seaside park around a granite star fort where locals walk the loop of Pleasure Bay, watch planes skim in to Logan and queue for hot dogs at Sullivan's.`,tip:`Walk the 3-kilometre Pleasure Bay causeway loop; the fort interior opens only for occasional summer tours.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Castle Island (Massachusetts)`},{id:`boston-childrens-museum`,name:`Boston Children's Museum`,category:`family`,tags:[`kids`,`rainy-day`,`interactive`],area:`Seaport`,lat:42.35184,lng:-71.04986,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:22,rating:3,description:`One of the oldest children's museums in the world, with a three-storey climbing maze, bubble room and construction zone, marked by the giant Hood milk bottle outside.`,tip:`Best for under-10s; book timed tickets for weekends and rainy school holidays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Boston Children's Museum`},{id:`arnold-arboretum`,name:`Arnold Arboretum`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`garden`,`walk`,`autumn-colours`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Jamaica Plain`,lat:42.30728,lng:-71.11998,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Harvard's free 114-hectare tree museum in the Emerald Necklace park chain, glorious with lilacs in May and blazing maples in October.`,tip:`Take the Orange Line to Forest Hills and walk up Peters Hill for a skyline view framed by trees.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Arnold Arboretum`},{id:`jfk-presidential-library`,name:`John F. Kennedy Presidential Library and Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`rainy-day`,`harbour-views`,`politics`],area:`Dorchester`,lat:42.31623,lng:-71.03403,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:18,rating:4,description:`I. M. Pei's striking white library on Columbia Point tells the story of JFK's life and presidency, ending in a soaring glass pavilion over the harbour.`,tip:`Ride the Red Line to JFK/UMass and take the free shuttle bus; allow time for the Cuban Missile Crisis gallery.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`John F. Kennedy Presidential Library and Museum`},{id:`wallys-cafe-jazz-club`,name:`Wally's Cafe Jazz Club`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`jazz`,`live-music`,`historic`,`late-night`],area:`South End`,lat:42.34256,lng:-71.08086,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:15,rating:4,description:`A tiny, packed jazz bar open since 1947, one of Boston's first Black-owned businesses, with live music every night and Berklee students jamming late.`,tip:`Usually no cover, but it is small and fills fast on weekends; arrive early for a spot near the band.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Wally's Cafe`},{id:`symphony-hall-boston`,name:`Symphony Hall`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`classical-music`,`concert`,`historic`,`iconic`],area:`Fenway`,lat:42.34262,lng:-71.08566,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:60,rating:4,description:`The 1900 home of the Boston Symphony Orchestra and the Boston Pops, revered as one of the finest concert halls in the world for its acoustics.`,tip:`The BSO season runs from autumn to spring and the Pops play in late spring and at the holidays; look for cheaper rush and under-40 tickets.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Symphony Hall (Boston)`},{id:`salem-day-trip`,name:`Salem`,category:`culture`,tags:[`day-trip`,`history`,`witch-trials`,`museum`,`halloween`],area:`Salem`,lat:42.51954,lng:-70.89672,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:4,description:`The seaport town of the 1692 witch trials, with a sober trials memorial, the House of the Seven Gables and the outstanding Peabody Essex Museum.`,tip:`Commuter rail from North Station takes about 30 minutes; in October it is mobbed for Halloween, so go early or on a weekday.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Salem, Massachusetts`},{id:`provincetown-day-trip`,name:`Provincetown (Cape Cod) by fast ferry`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`day-trip`,`beach`,`boat`,`cape-cod`,`summer`],area:`Provincetown`,lat:42.05008,lng:-70.1864,durationHours:9,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:110,rating:4,description:`A 90-minute fast ferry to the tip of Cape Cod, an arty, colourful fishing town of galleries, dunes and wide beaches where the Pilgrims first landed.`,tip:`Fast ferries leave from downtown wharves from about late May to mid-October; book ahead in summer, and rent a bike for the dune trails.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Provincetown, Massachusetts`},{id:`lexington-concord`,name:`Lexington and Concord (Minute Man National Historical Park)`,category:`culture`,tags:[`day-trip`,`history`,`revolution`,`cycling`,`free`],area:`Lexington and Concord`,lat:42.4688,lng:-71.351,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:4,description:`Where the first shots of the Revolution rang out in April 1775, from Lexington Battle Green along the Battle Road to Concord's Old North Bridge.`,tip:`Easiest by car; the commuter rail reaches Concord, where you can also visit Walden Pond and the homes of Emerson and Louisa May Alcott.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Minute Man National Historical Park`}],foods:[{name:`New England clam chowder`,description:`A creamy, milky soup of chopped clams, potatoes and salt pork, served with oyster crackers; the Boston way never includes tomato.`},{name:`Lobster roll`,description:`Chunks of sweet lobster in a buttered, toasted split-top bun, either cold with a light dressing of mayo or warm with melted butter.`},{name:`Fried clams`,description:`Whole-belly clams dipped in batter and deep-fried until crisp, served by the heap with tartar sauce at seaside clam shacks.`},{name:`Raw oysters`,description:`Briny, ice-cold local oysters from Duxbury, Wellfleet and Cape Cod, shucked to order at raw bars all over town.`},{name:`Cannoli`,description:`Crisp fried pastry tubes filled with sweet ricotta, the North End's favourite treat, sold in white string-tied boxes.`},{name:`Boston cream pie`,description:`Actually a cake: sponge layers filled with vanilla custard and glazed with chocolate, created at the Parker House hotel in the 1850s.`}]},{id:`honolulu`,name:`Honolulu`,lat:21.30694,lng:-157.85833,timezone:`Pacific/Honolulu`,tagline:`Waikīkī surf, volcanic craters and island aloha`,description:`Hawaiʻi's capital wraps Waikīkī's famous beach around the Diamond Head crater, with Pearl Harbor, the only royal palace on US soil and the treasures of the Bishop Museum close by. Beyond the city, Oʻahu offers turquoise snorkelling bays, ridge hikes, the windward beaches of Kailua and the big-wave North Shore. It is warm all year; winter brings big surf to the north and whales offshore, and several top sights need booking ahead.`,idealDays:[4,7],places:[{id:`waikiki-beach`,name:`Waikīkī Beach`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`iconic`,`beach`,`free`,`surf`,`sunset`],area:`Waikīkī`,lat:21.2753,lng:-157.825,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`A long crescent of golden sand backed by palms and hotels, with gentle rolling surf, outrigger canoes and Diamond Head rising at its eastern end.`,tip:`Kūhiō Beach, by the Duke Kahanamoku statue, has calm, walled-in swimming; stay for sunset, when the whole beach turns gold.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Waikīkī`},{id:`diamond-head`,name:`Diamond Head State Monument`,localName:`Lēʻahi`,category:`nature`,tags:[`iconic`,`hiking`,`viewpoint`,`crater`,`reservation`],area:`Diamond Head`,lat:21.2636,lng:-157.8058,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:5,rating:5,description:`A steep 1.3-kilometre trail climbs inside the rim of an ancient volcanic crater, through tunnels and up stairs to old military bunkers with sweeping views over Waikīkī.`,tip:`Visitors must book a timed entry slot online in advance (up to 30 days ahead); take the earliest slot to beat the heat and bring water, as there is little shade.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Diamond Head, Hawaii`},{id:`hanauma-bay`,name:`Hanauma Bay Nature Preserve`,category:`nature`,tags:[`iconic`,`snorkelling`,`beach`,`reef`,`reservation`],area:`East Oʻahu`,lat:21.2691,lng:-157.6938,durationHours:3.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:5,description:`A turquoise bay inside a collapsed volcanic crater, its protected coral reef teeming with parrotfish, tangs and green sea turtles a few strokes from the sand.`,tip:`Reservations are needed: they open online two days ahead at 7am Hawaiʻi time and go in minutes. Closed Mondays and Tuesdays; everyone watches a short reef-safety video first.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Hanauma Bay`},{id:`pearl-harbor-national-memorial`,name:`Pearl Harbor National Memorial (USS Arizona)`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`history`,`ww2`,`memorial`],area:`Pearl Harbor`,lat:21.3678,lng:-157.9387,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:1,rating:5,description:`A moving memorial to the 7 December 1941 attack, with museums at the visitor centre and a Navy boat out to the white memorial straddling the sunken USS Arizona.`,tip:`The memorial program is free but book timed tickets online (a small booking fee) up to eight weeks ahead; bags are not allowed, so bring only a clear pouch or use the storage.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Pearl Harbor National Memorial`},{id:`battleship-missouri`,name:`Battleship Missouri Memorial`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`ww2`,`ship`,`kids`],area:`Pearl Harbor`,lat:21.3625,lng:-157.9541,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:4,description:`The "Mighty Mo", on whose deck Japan surrendered in 1945, now moored on Ford Island so you can roam its decks, gun turrets and crew quarters.`,tip:`Reached by shuttle bus from the Pearl Harbor visitor centre; pair it with the USS Arizona Memorial for a full morning.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`USS Missouri (BB-63)`},{id:`pearl-harbor-aviation-museum`,name:`Pearl Harbor Aviation Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`aircraft`,`rainy-day`,`kids`],area:`Pearl Harbor`,lat:21.3598,lng:-157.9612,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:28,rating:3,description:`Historic WWII hangars on Ford Island, one still scarred by bullet holes from the attack, filled with fighters, bombers and flight simulators.`,tip:`Also reached by the Ford Island shuttle; buy a combination ticket with the Missouri if you plan both.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Pearl Harbor Aviation Museum`},{id:`iolani-palace`,name:`ʻIolani Palace`,category:`culture`,tags:[`history`,`royal`,`rainy-day`,`architecture`],area:`Downtown`,lat:21.3066,lng:-157.8587,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`The only royal palace in the United States, home of Hawaiʻi's last monarchs, King Kalākaua and Queen Liliʻuokalani, restored with its koa-wood staircase and throne room.`,tip:`Book a guided or audio tour online, as slots sell out; check opening days, as it is closed some days of the week. The gold-leafed King Kamehameha statue stands across the street.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`ʻIolani Palace`},{id:`capitol-modern`,name:`Capitol Modern (Hawaiʻi State Art Museum)`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`art`,`rainy-day`,`local-artists`],area:`Downtown`,lat:21.3086,lng:-157.8589,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The state's free museum of art by Hawaiʻi artists, in a Spanish Mission-style building a short walk from ʻIolani Palace, with a sculpture garden behind.`,tip:`Open Wednesday to Saturday daytimes only; on First Fridays it stays open into the evening with music.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Capitol Modern`},{id:`bishop-museum`,name:`Bishop Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`iconic`,`culture`,`hawaiian-history`,`rainy-day`,`kids`],area:`Kalihi`,lat:21.3333,lng:-157.8707,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:5,description:`The world's finest collection of Hawaiian and Polynesian culture, with royal feather capes, carved gods and canoes in the three-storey koa-panelled Hawaiian Hall.`,tip:`Allow time for the planetarium show and the science hall; it is a 15-minute drive or bus ride from downtown.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Bishop Museum`},{id:`honolulu-museum-of-art`,name:`Honolulu Museum of Art`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`rainy-day`,`courtyard`,`asian-art`],area:`Makiki`,lat:21.3038,lng:-157.8485,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:4,description:`A serene museum of open-air courtyards and galleries spanning Asian, Pacific, European and American art, from Hokusai prints to Van Gogh.`,tip:`Check opening days, as it is closed part of the week; the courtyard cafe is a lovely lunch stop.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Honolulu Museum of Art`},{id:`chinatown-honolulu`,name:`Chinatown`,category:`food`,tags:[`food`,`lei-stands`,`markets`,`bars`,`art`],area:`Chinatown`,lat:21.312,lng:-157.8623,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`Historic low-rise streets of lei sellers, noodle shops, fish markets and dim sum by day, and some of the city's best cocktail bars and restaurants after dark.`,tip:`Come on the first Friday of the month for the evening art walk; stick to the busier streets at night.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Chinatown, Honolulu`},{id:`foster-botanical-garden`,name:`Foster Botanical Garden`,category:`nature`,tags:[`garden`,`trees`,`hidden-gem`,`quiet`],area:`Chinatown`,lat:21.317,lng:-157.859,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:5,rating:3,description:`A calm, shady garden on the edge of Chinatown with towering exceptional trees, orchids and palms planted since the 1850s.`,tip:`Pick up the self-guided map at the entrance; mosquitoes can be keen, so bring repellent.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Foster Botanical Garden`},{id:`kakaako-murals`,name:`Kakaʻako street art`,category:`culture`,tags:[`free`,`street-art`,`photo`,`cafes`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Kakaʻako`,lat:21.2969,lng:-157.8588,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A former warehouse district covered in giant, colourful murals from the annual POW! WOW! festival, now dotted with breweries, cafes and the SALT shops.`,tip:`Wander the blocks around Auahi and Cooke streets, then cross to Kakaʻako Waterfront Park for sea views.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Kakaʻako`},{id:`ala-moana-center`,name:`Ala Moana Center`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`shopping`,`rainy-day`,`food-court`,`free`],area:`Ala Moana`,lat:21.2911,lng:-157.8433,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`One of the world's largest open-air shopping centres, with hundreds of shops, a big Japanese food hall and Ala Moana Beach Park across the road.`,tip:`Free entry; walk across to Ala Moana Beach Park and Magic Island for a calm swim and sunset.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Ala Moana Center`},{id:`international-market-place`,name:`International Market Place`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`shopping`,`banyan-tree`,`free`,`evening`],area:`Waikīkī`,lat:21.2789,lng:-157.8268,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A tiered open-air shopping centre on Kalākaua Avenue built around a huge, century-old banyan tree, with shops and restaurants on its upper decks.`,tip:`Head to the upper level's Grand Lanai for dining with a view over the banyan.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`International Market Place`},{id:`waikiki-surf-lesson`,name:`Surf lesson at Waikīkī`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`surf`,`beach`,`active`,`lesson`],area:`Waikīkī`,lat:21.2761,lng:-157.8268,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:90,rating:4,description:`Learn to surf on the slow, rolling waves where Duke Kahanamoku popularised the sport, with beach instructors pushing you into your first ride.`,tip:`Book a small-group lesson with one of the beach stands near the Duke statue; mornings bring calmer winds, and wear reef-safe sunscreen.`,indoor:!1},{id:`waikiki-sunset-sail`,name:`Waikīkī sunset catamaran sail`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`boat`,`sunset`,`night-view`,`drinks`],area:`Waikīkī`,lat:21.2777,lng:-157.8299,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:60,rating:4,description:`Catamarans run right off the sand for a 90-minute sail along the coast, with Diamond Head and the Waikīkī skyline glowing at sunset.`,tip:`Boats depart from the beach in front of the big hotels; on Fridays, pick a later sail that lines up with the Hilton fireworks.`,indoor:!1},{id:`hilton-friday-fireworks`,name:`Friday fireworks at Hilton Hawaiian Village`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`free`,`fireworks`,`night-view`,`kids`],area:`Waikīkī`,lat:21.281,lng:-157.8379,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A short, free fireworks show bursts over the beach at the western end of Waikīkī every Friday night, a long-running local tradition.`,tip:`It starts around 7:45 or 8pm depending on the season and lasts about 10 minutes; watch from the sand near the Duke Kahanamoku Lagoon.`,indoor:!1},{id:`kuhio-beach-hula-show`,name:`Kūhiō Beach Hula Show`,category:`culture`,tags:[`free`,`hula`,`music`,`sunset`,`kids`],area:`Waikīkī`,lat:21.2745,lng:-157.8245,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A free open-air show of traditional hula and Hawaiian music at the beachside Hula Mound, starting with a torch lighting and conch shell call at sunset.`,tip:`Usually held on Saturday evenings around 6 to 6:30pm, weather permitting; check the current schedule and bring a mat to sit on the grass.`,indoor:!1},{id:`house-without-a-key`,name:`House Without a Key`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`sunset`,`hula`,`cocktails`,`live-music`,`iconic`],area:`Waikīkī`,lat:21.2786,lng:-157.8329,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`The Halekulani hotel's oceanfront terrace, where a hula dancer performs to Hawaiian music under an old kiawe tree as the sun sets behind it.`,tip:`Arrive an hour before sunset for a seat with a view; order a mai tai and stay for the music.`,indoor:!1},{id:`blue-note-hawaii`,name:`Blue Note Hawaii`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`jazz`,`live-music`,`rainy-day`,`concert`],area:`Waikīkī`,lat:21.2778,lng:-157.8285,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:3,description:`An intimate supper club in the Outrigger Waikīkī hotel hosting jazz, Hawaiian music and touring acts most nights, from ukulele virtuosos to soul legends.`,tip:`Buy tickets ahead and arrive early, as seating is first come, first served; there is a food-and-drink minimum per person.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Blue Note Hawaii`},{id:`waikiki-aquarium`,name:`Waikīkī Aquarium`,category:`family`,tags:[`aquarium`,`kids`,`rainy-day`,`reef`],area:`Waikīkī`,lat:21.2657,lng:-157.8217,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`One of the oldest public aquariums in the US, small but excellent, focused on Hawaiian reef life, with monk seals, jellyfish and living corals.`,tip:`An easy stop at the Diamond Head end of Kapiʻolani Park; combine with the zoo nearby.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Waikīkī Aquarium`},{id:`honolulu-zoo`,name:`Honolulu Zoo`,category:`family`,tags:[`zoo`,`kids`],area:`Waikīkī`,lat:21.2712,lng:-157.821,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:21,rating:3,description:`A leafy zoo on the edge of Kapiʻolani Park with an African savannah, Komodo dragons and native Hawaiian birds like the nēnē goose.`,tip:`Go early, when animals are most active and before the midday heat.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Honolulu Zoo`},{id:`kcc-farmers-market`,name:`KCC Farmers' Market`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`local-food`,`breakfast`,`weekend`],area:`Diamond Head`,lat:21.2708,lng:-157.8014,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`A lively Saturday-morning farmers' market at Kapiʻolani Community College, packed with tropical fruit, abalone, fresh juices and local breakfast plates.`,tip:`Saturdays from 7:30am to around 11am; arrive early, then hike Diamond Head nearby if you hold an early slot.`,indoor:!1},{id:`manoa-falls`,name:`Mānoa Falls Trail`,category:`nature`,tags:[`hiking`,`waterfall`,`rainforest`],area:`Mānoa`,lat:21.3328,lng:-157.8005,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:7,rating:4,description:`A 2.6-kilometre round-trip walk through dripping rainforest of banyans, bamboo and ginger to a tall, slender waterfall in the valley behind the city.`,tip:`The trail is often muddy, so wear shoes with grip and bring repellent; there is a paid parking lot at the trailhead.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Mānoa Falls`},{id:`nuuanu-pali-lookout`,name:`Nuʻuanu Pali Lookout`,category:`nature`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`history`,`windy`],area:`Nuʻuanu`,lat:21.3666,lng:-157.7934,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:7,rating:4,description:`A wind-blasted lookout on the sheer cliffs of the Koʻolau range, gazing over the green windward coast, where Kamehameha won the battle that united Oʻahu in 1795.`,tip:`A quick stop on the drive to Kailua; non-residents pay a parking fee, and bring a layer, as the wind is fierce.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Nuʻuanu Pali`},{id:`koko-crater-stairs`,name:`Koko Crater Stairs`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`hiking`,`free`,`viewpoint`,`workout`],area:`East Oʻahu`,lat:21.2815,lng:-157.6922,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A punishing climb of over a thousand old railway ties straight up the side of Koko Crater, rewarded with views over Hanauma Bay and the east coast.`,tip:`Start at sunrise to avoid the heat; there is no shade, and the middle section crosses an open trestle.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Koko Crater`},{id:`halona-blowhole`,name:`Hālona Blowhole Lookout`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`viewpoint`,`coast`,`whales`],area:`East Oʻahu`,lat:21.2832,lng:-157.6771,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A roadside lookout where waves force sea spray up through a lava tube with a whoosh, beside a tiny cove made famous by the film From Here to Eternity.`,tip:`Stay on the lookout; the rocks below are dangerous. In winter, scan the horizon for humpback whales.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Hālona Blowhole`},{id:`makapuu-lighthouse-trail`,name:`Makapuʻu Point Lighthouse Trail`,category:`nature`,tags:[`hiking`,`free`,`viewpoint`,`whales`,`kids`],area:`East Oʻahu`,lat:21.3029,lng:-157.6506,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A paved trail of about 3 kilometres round trip up to clifftop views of a red-roofed lighthouse, offshore islets and the turquoise windward coast.`,tip:`Easy but completely exposed, so go early with water and sun protection; humpback whales pass from December to April.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Makapuʻu Point`},{id:`kailua-lanikai-beaches`,name:`Kailua and Lanikai beaches`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`beach`,`free`,`kayaking`,`snorkelling`],area:`Kailua`,lat:21.3979,lng:-157.7276,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Soft white sand and pale turquoise water on the windward side, where you can kayak from Kailua Beach out to the Mokulua islets off neighbouring Lanikai.`,tip:`Park at Kailua Beach Park, as Lanikai has very little parking; the short Lanikai Pillbox hike above gives the classic view of the islets.`,indoor:!1},{id:`byodo-in-temple`,name:`Byodo-In Temple`,category:`culture`,tags:[`temple`,`garden`,`peaceful`,`photo`],area:`Kāneʻohe`,lat:21.4309,lng:-157.8319,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:5,rating:3,description:`A scarlet replica of a 950-year-old Japanese temple set against the sheer green cliffs of the Koʻolau range, with koi ponds and a great bronze peace bell.`,tip:`It sits inside the Valley of the Temples cemetery; ring the bell for good luck and combine it with Kailua.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Byodo-In`},{id:`kualoa-ranch`,name:`Kualoa Ranch`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`day-trip`,`movie-sets`,`atv`,`horse-riding`,`kids`],area:`Kualoa`,lat:21.5209,lng:-157.8369,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:80,rating:4,description:`A vast private ranch in a dramatic valley on the windward coast, the backdrop for Jurassic Park and dozens of films, explored by bus, ATV, horseback or zipline.`,tip:`Book tours well ahead, especially the movie-site and UTV tours; the drive from Waikīkī takes about 45 minutes.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Kualoa Ranch`},{id:`north-shore-haleiwa`,name:`North Shore and Haleʻiwa`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`surf`,`beach`,`turtles`,`shave-ice`],area:`North Shore`,lat:21.5931,lng:-158.1036,durationHours:8,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:4,description:`Laid-back surf town Haleʻiwa, with its shave-ice shops and garlic-shrimp trucks, leads to legendary beaches like Waimea Bay, Sunset Beach and the Banzai Pipeline.`,tip:`Winter brings giant waves for watching, not swimming; in summer the sea is calm enough to snorkel at Waimea and Shark's Cove. Look for turtles at Laniākea.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Haleʻiwa, Hawaii`},{id:`polynesian-cultural-center`,name:`Polynesian Cultural Center`,category:`culture`,tags:[`day-trip`,`culture`,`luau`,`kids`,`show`],area:`Lāʻie`,lat:21.639,lng:-157.9206,durationHours:7,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:95,rating:4,description:`Villages representing Samoa, Tonga, Fiji, Tahiti, Aotearoa and Hawaiʻi, with canoe pageants, fire-knife dancing and a big evening show, staffed largely by Pacific Island students.`,tip:`Closed Sundays; arrive by early afternoon to see the village demonstrations before the luau and night show.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Polynesian Cultural Center`}],foods:[{name:`Poke`,description:`Cubes of raw ahi tuna or octopus tossed with shoyu, sesame oil, sea salt, seaweed and onion, bought by the pound at markets and eaten over rice.`},{name:`Plate lunch`,description:`Hawaiʻi's everyday meal: two scoops of rice, a scoop of macaroni salad and a main such as teriyaki beef, garlic chicken or kalbi ribs.`},{name:`Loco moco`,description:`A hamburger patty on rice, topped with a fried egg and smothered in brown gravy, invented in Hilo in the 1940s.`},{name:`Kalua pig`,localName:`Kālua puaʻa`,description:`Smoky, salty shredded pork traditionally slow-cooked in an underground imu oven, served with poi, lomi salmon and laulau.`},{name:`Shave ice`,description:`Ice shaved as fine as snow and drenched in tropical syrups like lilikoʻi and li hing mui, often with ice cream or azuki beans hidden underneath.`},{name:`Malasada`,description:`A Portuguese-style doughnut without a hole, fried to order and rolled in sugar, sometimes filled with haupia coconut custard.`}]}]};export{e as unitedStates};